:"carousel","platform":"instagram","source_url":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAY9PWFuEX/","excerpt":"Link: https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAY9PWFuEX/ Slide 13 of 16 Text on it: 33 words, 9% of the area. Colours: #4f4b49 16%, #0f0c0a 16%, #7c7a7f 10%, #441f13 6%, #b4abaf 6% Text: im oe re WAI Fs WILL FIRST PLACE IN THE WORLD WHERE POLI ING DURING ELECTIONS WILL BE A CRIMINAL OFFEN…","created_at":"2026-10-28T06:03:52.795035+00:00"},{"id":"611a1c3c-e9cd-4cec-948b-d2c7d97af2a0","title":"instagram_DfAY9PWFuEX_15.jpg","shape":"carousel","platform":"instagram","source_url":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAY9PWFuEX/","excerpt":"Link: https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAY9PWFuEX/ Slide 15 of 16 Text on it: 23 words, 8% of the area. Colours: #070809 25%, #444c4d 8%, #174550 7%, #7f817b 5%, #4c777e 5% Text: So JAPAN HAS ACHIEVED A RECORD INTERNET SPEED: 1.02 PETABITS PER SECOND, ALLOWING YOU TO DOWNLOAD ALL OF…","created_at":"2026-10-28T06:03:52.795035+00:00"}],"creators":[{"id":"56e4e1e8-afbd-4134-995a-78f7b17572c0","creator":"andreas-horn","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/andreashorn1_something-changed-in-the-last-few-months-activity-7522313115103825920-on2o","why_it_works":"It takes the obvious observation that agents got better and redirects the entire argument to organizational design, which is a more durable and less covered claim than another capability update.","krish_angle":"Krish's agentic operating system did not get faster when the models did, because the approval stack he inherited from a human-run business was still five layers deep; the actual unlock came from deleting three of those layers and publishing what broke when he did it.","idea_id":"21b424c2-8bad-4937-9daf-9e3e366f101f","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:01:18.009568+00:00"},{"id":"6a5cffe3-9e64-4bf6-979d-527f207d707e","creator":"andreas-horn","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/andreashorn1_the-question-i-get-most-from-engineering-activity-7521846495101452288-vk52","why_it_works":"It reframes a resourcing question as a structural one, then earns it with specific before/after ratios from one real org rather than an industry survey, which makes the claim feel inspected rather than asserted.","krish_angle":"The handoff is the unit that breaks, not the headcount, and Krish's own agent fleet proves it differently: his bottleneck is not model output but how many of his own review gates a single human can staff before judgment becomes the rate limiter, with the actual gate-to-output ratio from his build published.","idea_id":"715de6f4-8325-498a-8457-025969eec9a6","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:01:17.66438+00:00"},{"id":"bc8533e1-3d51-47b0-bd36-3b7dddd5aa39","creator":"alex-lieberman","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alex-lieberman_tenex-agent-bootcamp-register-your-interest-activity-7519085253894795266-riNr","why_it_works":"the numbered list of specific, sometimes contradictory lessons reads as field notes rather than a pitch, which earns trust that a polished case study would not","krish_angle":"Krish's angle is the one lesson Lieberman's list skips: automating a function instead of a person only compounds if someone owns the handoff between functions, and in the 20-person agentic operating model that owner is usually the founder by default, which is a bottleneck nobody is pricing into the build","idea_id":"49f1b207-e0c2-4163-812d-d71c53c8154a","created_at":"2026-10-27T08:01:04.946479+00:00"},{"id":"9f36eaf9-1534-4f08-be42-16aac998f7d9","creator":"justin-kramm","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/justinkramm_if-we-automate-the-career-ladder-whos-going-activity-7518776535844179969-ySym","why_it_works":"it compresses a real worry about skill formation into eleven words everyone already has stored in memory, so the reader supplies the argument themselves","krish_angle":"Krish's version is not nostalgia for craft, it is a specific claim about agentic ops: the repetitive grunt work that used to train junior judgment is exactly the work founders are now handing to agents first, which means the skill gap will show up in year three, not year one, and nobody is tracking it","idea_id":"beb36a77-50d0-4e78-833b-81fa4b91147c","created_at":"2026-10-27T08:01:04.433218+00:00"},{"id":"dede7cf0-25fd-4164-9ad3-7c924fc861f1","creator":"alex-lieberman","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alex-lieberman_you-pay-20-a-month-for-claude-where-does-activity-7518844441378521088-kZBl","why_it_works":"nobody has itemised their own subscription bill this way, so it converts an abstract industry (AI infrastructure) into something as legible as a grocery receipt, which makes the economics feel real instead of theoretical","krish_angle":"Krish can do the same breakdown one layer up: not what Anthropic does with your $20, but what his own portfolio spends per task when an agent fleet runs it versus what the same task cost with a human contractor last year, itemised the same way: model calls, orchestration overhead, human review minutes, output rework.","idea_id":"aaf688c7-fd7b-4d86-ab74-c83bd0cb9426","created_at":"2026-10-24T06:39:07.567785+00:00"},{"id":"86344152-1282-4cd7-abb8-0261e49e3b24","creator":"alex-lieberman","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alex-lieberman_im-sick-of-reading-ai-slop-so-today-im-activity-7519476473389527041-Z5kf","why_it_works":"it turns a vague complaint everyone has into a measurable thing with a checklist and data, which makes the complaint actionable instead of just relatable","krish_angle":"Krish's agentic operating system already produces thousands of agent outputs a week. The real cost of AI content is not slop detection, it is slop liability: who signs off when an agent's output ships under a human name. He can publish the actual approval gate his fleet uses before anything goes external, with the rejection rate from the last 30 days.","idea_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-24T06:39:07.236226+00:00"},{"id":"2527164a-6633-462d-a548-a4ade6a5e2c2","creator":"alex-lieberman","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alex-lieberman_just-had-lunch-with-a-strategy-exec-at-a-activity-7503966729509883904-LPRA","why_it_works":"It resolves a real, unglamorous org design question with a memorable two-word framework that is immediately applicable and testable inside any company reading it.","krish_angle":"Krish's version rejects the premise that AI needs a single human owner at all once a company is running agent fleets. The real question in his world is not who owns AI, it is which decisions the fleet is allowed to make without a human in the loop, and that org chart problem has no boss-and-bulldozer answer because the fleet itself is the organization now.","idea_id":"eadab090-1b63-46de-b957-9209c69bfcf2","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:01:32.545428+00:00"},{"id":"a7b3826e-f722-4596-a1e0-c2f6be4ecc46","creator":"alex-lieberman","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alex-lieberman_talk-nerdy-to-me-matt-shumer-the-gauntlet-activity-7505393630812135424-9coG","why_it_works":"It sells process, not output. The virality is the hook but the actual payload is a named, reusable loop that generalizes beyond the demo, which is what makes people show up to watch it live.","krish_angle":"Krish's agentic ops thesis is about the operating loop, not the demo. His differentiated version names the loop he actually runs to ship weekly builds solo and shows the failure points a viral demo never shows, because the real story is what breaks on the third run, not the first.","idea_id":null,"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:01:32.045495+00:00"},{"id":"f651f37f-199d-4fe7-b1d5-a68ab35aef4c","creator":"andreas-horn","post_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/andreashorn1_there-is-a-large-gap-between-how-people-talk-activity-7504458491592544257-ke-z","why_it_works":"It draws a hard, checkable line between fake agents and real ones using four testable criteria, then proves the framework with a number nobody can dispute: 21 agents, one operator, named tasks.","krish_angle":"Krish's differentiated cut is that the four capabilities are necessary but not sufficient. He can name the fifth thing that breaks agent fleets even when tools, context, memory, and initiative are all present: the absence of an escalation contract, meaning nobody defined what the agent is allowed to decide alone versus what it must kick upstairs, and that gap is where his fleet actually failed.","idea_id":"5dc3d87f-3758-4640-8bb6-9a301961bc87","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:01:31.679916+00:00"}],"claims":[{"id":"b0b400d5-35bb-4f4a-93cd-47a2469c597d","layer":"graphics","status":"proposed","statement":"He rejects cluttered, cramped, or hierarchy-confused layouts, overlapping components, walls of text, or logos and badges competing with the headline, insisting every card stay clean, spacious, and headline-led.","his_words":"The headline should take precedence.","support":7},{"id":"95f17c54-ec7d-4eaa-a9b9-ac66fe623ee4","layer":"tone","status":"proposed","statement":"He rejects a piece or format the moment it feels boring to him, regardless of how well-executed or technically correct it otherwise is.","his_words":"It's so boring.","support":8},{"id":"c4a48148-b3e4-42a1-a396-31b0f89a4d80","layer":"packaging","status":"proposed","statement":"He wants the word mark and brand marks kept small, tucked in a consistent corner, and removed from vertical shorts where they aren't needed.","his_words":"small \"Make Your Mind Up\" word mark, bottom-right aligned","support":5},{"id":"d4e47dca-e899-475a-b82d-91d6cbceca5e","layer":"production","status":"proposed","statement":"He treats every video and graphic against a floor standard of premium, cinematic production quality, rejecting anything that looks cheap, amateurish, or low-budget.","his_words":"premium quality, motion design, cinematic feeling, movement, branding","support":6},{"id":"9c75ab7c-be7a-486e-824a-54adb4854026","layer":"camerawork","status":"proposed","statement":"He wants caption placement to be a deliberate, thoughtful choice that never covers his face or sits awkwardly over a split screen.","his_words":"be thoughtful as to where captions go (and do not go)","support":6},{"id":"944e12dc-646b-46c4-a8bb-ee3fb907523a","layer":"opening","status":"proposed","statement":"He prefers titles and headings that hold back the key twist or finding as a question or surprising reveal, rather than stating the answer outright.","his_words":null,"support":6},{"id":"03f25f8f-2f4d-4ca0-9cd1-21eb101cdb3c","layer":"tone","status":"proposed","statement":"He rejects any line that doesn't make clear sense when read aloud, including vague pronouns like 'it' or 'the company' that leave the listener unsure what's being referenced.","his_words":"the companys computers\" makes no sense","support":8},{"id":"b0b7764e-ecfb-4f62-a25b-1c1f7d33cfcf","layer":"packaging","status":"proposed","statement":"He approves a title only after seeing it alongside the finished video, in one packaging pass, not before.","his_words":"Use this set (Recommended)","support":5},{"id":"4b77c851-1226-4d72-8f5d-5dffe726d4f0","layer":"packaging","status":"proposed","statement":"He rejects insider shorthand or jargon that only makes sense to someone who already has context, insisting every audience-facing line name the real thing in plain words.","his_words":"They're offensive to me. They hurt my soul.","support":5},{"id":"a0269b13-b3e3-4cdc-a7a4-b4c62f84b6f3","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants on-screen visuals to carry most of the explanation, matching every spoken analogy and increasing visual density proportionally when the cut speeds up.","his_words":"the 90 second video needs to have visuals nearly the entire way through as when things are sped up, we need to 3-5X the visual clarity","support":4},{"id":"37404281-53e3-4504-985a-566cc58c6fe5","layer":"tone","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants scripts to include short, dry, deadpan wit and sarcasm built from true details, not a flat recitation of results.","his_words":"Bit of dry wit and hannah fry sarcasm too","support":3},{"id":"9b31c66f-5775-4bc1-abd2-801ff091838a","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants captions designed with bold, unique, art-directed styling, rejecting plain, boring, or under-animated default caption treatments.","his_words":"The captions are very unique and well-designed, like an art director would do them","support":4},{"id":"2740c46f-2f6e-41b5-9b77-c8e2958f0544","layer":"packaging","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants thumbnails purposefully designed with more than just a face on a plain background, matching curated style references rather than defaulting to a flat look.","his_words":"They usually don't have just the authors face in them and usually not juts a black background","support":3},{"id":"86383f00-51e2-407c-a8d0-9e7367e7af34","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He insists any generated likeness of a real person, his own or others, stay accurate and clearly recognizable, rejecting caricatures or renders that distort proportions or fail to resemble the actual person.","his_words":"We can't generate caricatures that people won't recognize clearly.","support":5},{"id":"8df979f4-9ac6-4c95-b271-a34925b84171","layer":"packaging","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants a carousel's cover card to be visually sensational and distinct from the rest of the set, announcing itself as the cover, rather than plain, screenshot-only, or blending in with other cards.","his_words":"For both covers the image needs to be more absurd, hilarious, and creative.","support":5},{"id":"198391fc-4fe8-4233-bc28-123a9e824797","layer":"structure","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants each carousel card to carry a clear, self-contained point that makes sense without assumed context, rejecting cryptic copy that relies on prior knowledge or too few words.","his_words":"The cards cannot be cryptic at all.","support":3},{"id":"2a639bac-30b0-4b84-9a21-da4430209c9e","layer":"camerawork","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants eye-contact and eye-gaze correction applied strongly and consistently across every final render, not left subtle, inconsistent, or unfixed.","his_words":"make it stronger, the eye contact needs to be visible","support":4},{"id":"8c5bd88a-c0e7-45f5-8b5f-b432d7e7773f","layer":"tone","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects content that feels generic or interchangeable, insisting every piece reflect his specific brand voice, reference library, and established style rather than default template output.","his_words":"you've just met me for the first time and produced some piece of shit that you would produce for anyone","support":3},{"id":"857d0645-afea-4a38-a807-c64b2ed5f965","layer":"proof","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants proof and examples grounded in real, concrete, sourced material, actual screenshots, named stories, real data, rather than placeholder mocks, generic illustrations, or unsupported assertions.","his_words":"Impossible to really tell what I'm approving with these mocks.","support":6},{"id":"02241d5d-1c0e-4ffe-b845-08e8e74b2c15","layer":"proof","status":"candidate","statement":"He insists punchy titles and quoted lines stay strictly accurate to the real underlying facts and reporting, correcting or rejecting phrasing that oversells or misstates what actually happened even when it reads better.","his_words":"wording corrected for truth by the session","support":2},{"id":"3549faf5-f012-4f02-bc16-7da51bc1ac04","layer":"tone","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants his cloned voice to sound authentically like his real speaking voice, matching his natural accent, pace and articulation, correcting any version that sounds crisper, posher, differently accented or mismatched in speed.","his_words":"Fuck me, I am now northern, gay and posh","support":5},{"id":"2180638c-ba6b-4b40-ba14-97b0131d53fd","layer":"close","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects mandatory formats like predictions being forced into every piece, wanting such devices used only when he specifically calls for them on that particular piece.","his_words":"it's baseless, lame and has no value","support":3},{"id":"5d30c676-f5b7-49bb-a229-c9dc02295f93","layer":"tone","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants genuine humor and fun treated as a non-negotiable baseline for every piece, not an optional stylistic extra.","his_words":"makeyourmindup should always have good humour","support":6},{"id":"8cad2e3a-d044-49ce-ade0-1f49de8e8581","layer":"camerawork","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants camera framing kept tight on his face with no wasted empty space beside him, and rejects any overlay or split-screen element that blocks or covers his face.","his_words":"I dont need to be leaving so much sofa space next to me","support":3},{"id":"49ee17b6-a04a-4b37-80a6-a871cd8d4b8e","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants headline typography to stick to his established brand fonts (like Anton capitals), rejecting generic or overused AI-style fonts and off-brand font drift.","his_words":"instrument serif is over used in AI production, stick to BRAND","support":4},{"id":"5759ddcf-cf72-4f39-8b2d-aba6292c0332","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects self-referential disclaimer text, asterisks, or labels like 'generated by AI' and 'Krish's take' cluttering the content, insisting every visual serve the message directly.","his_words":"\"generated by AI\" and \"Krish's take\"","support":4},{"id":"b3e463a3-2a0b-438b-a1dd-d6cf6cbcd01f","layer":"production","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants background music kept audible throughout a piece at a low level under his voice, rising only at marked moments like intros, outros, or endings, rather than vanishing or staying silent.","his_words":"my voice is the main character","support":4},{"id":"4df72639-e368-44c2-a8b2-c78dbdd3ebe1","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects motion design and animation that feels slow, static, or under-stimulating, insisting on fast, dynamic, immersive movement.","his_words":"the motion is 10X too slow, not immersive and engaging at all","support":3},{"id":"504b7fa9-96fb-4ee2-ae68-182ee6b31b5a","layer":"opening","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants the opening frame to be visually powerful and legible, not a plain background or a flash that's gone before the viewer can register it.","his_words":"the first few seconds are kind of important","support":4},{"id":"e1ed6ded-0dbe-441d-87c0-de609d66612d","layer":"graphics","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects video layouts and animations that get cropped or fail to use the full screen, insisting every frame fill the available space.","his_words":"make maximum use of the full screen","support":4},{"id":"affc8d64-8e20-41de-8450-0e8fe23c9157","layer":"opening","status":"candidate","statement":"He favors short, punchy, imperative titles that state the lesson directly for learnings and tips content, rather than descriptive or vague labels.","his_words":null,"support":7},{"id":"0b7b6ddd-5f6a-4a6a-8479-cde06cd000e5","layer":"tone","status":"candidate","statement":"He calibrates content to real business leaders running mid-size companies, rejecting both examples pitched below them (mum-and-dad shops) and explanations that assume expert-level prior knowledge.","his_words":"My customers are medium sized enterprises.","support":4},{"id":"7bf329f3-fd56-4776-b8f6-9ab7a2a3e67c","layer":"packaging","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects packaging or headlines that single out one specific country or group as the suspect example when the piece's actual point is a pattern shared by many countries or parties.","his_words":"Sounds incredibly racist.","support":3},{"id":"d013c48b-2ad6-4a8a-b8bb-c8332f36df41","layer":"close","status":"candidate","statement":"He rejects a piece whose closing action, takeaway, or topic introduction repeats one already used in another recent piece, insisting each piece surface something genuinely new.","his_words":"I don't want every single takeaway to be \"go and look at your contract\"","support":3},{"id":"c3433913-73cb-42f0-9dae-3751426b4bb5","layer":"breakdown","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants the money trail behind a monetization or vertical-integration idea traced out explicitly, step by step, rather than left as a restated slogan.","his_words":"I think we need to really clearly visualize and unpick where the money goes","support":3},{"id":"b279130d-e787-433a-920d-756e30ca3cf6","layer":"production","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants background music kept at a consistent, steady volume that never cuts out, drops low, or jumps loud unpredictably, treating any such volatility as unprofessional.","his_words":"It's not professional at all.","support":4},{"id":"3900bbd9-9bf5-4b70-b029-2ec15026c9b3","layer":"breakdown","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants each party's distinct motive in a multi-company or multi-party story unpacked separately, not lumped into one general explanation.","his_words":"Why is Disney going after it, and why is Google going after it? They're two totally different companies. Unpack both.","support":4},{"id":"0bb1f79d-cbbb-4d53-87a1-3b21d2b28773","layer":"structure","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants the piece's overarching end message and checkpoints locked and signed off before production begins, and judges every edit against that fixed story rather than just its surface wording.","his_words":"I want to be crystal clear on the overarching end message and checkpoints of the piece so that we can't randomly go off track and take ages to iterate","support":3},{"id":"3271695b-5c0a-4ea3-bfb3-62dffed29843","layer":"production","status":"candidate","statement":"He wants a maintained bank of distinct edit and visual styles to draw from and keep upgrading production quality, rather than reusing one fixed template.","his_words":"I think we need to upgrade everything. And like be