unt":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DWv5XYPDffo/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"A $6 game on Steam is teaching people how data centers actually work, and it is getting attention fast.","excerpt":"A $6 game on Steam is teaching people how data centers actually work, and it is getting attention fast. The game is called Data Center. You start with empty floors and build from scratch. Buy racks, mount servers, route every cable by hand. The goal is to design and manage a functioning data center that handles real customer traffic. What makes it stand out is how it visualizes network activity.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DWtVKNPgF1g/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Someone rebuilt GeoGuessr, but instead of guessing where you are, you’re trying to figure out when you are.","excerpt":"Someone rebuilt GeoGuessr, but instead of guessing where you are, you’re trying to figure out when you are. Using GPT-Image-2, it generates full 360° environments from different eras, letting you drop into scenes that were never photographed or recorded. You move through spaces that feel like Street View, but set in ancient cities, lost moments, or entirely imagined timelines. There are no maps","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DX9c9OsDVm6/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨👀 Another major week in AI!","excerpt":"🚨👀 Another major week in AI! Here’s what’s new in the last 7 days: - Sci-Hub built ChatGPT for pirated science papers - Gemini can finally make real files in chat - Claude just plugged into the apps creatives actually use - Chinese humanoids are now sorting packages 24/7 - This AI thinks it’s still 1930 - Warp open-sourced its AI terminal, with OpenAI paying the bill - Cursor opened up the engine","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DX6hRlMjY6f/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"t