/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Resident Evil 4 but every single thing that ever made you panic has been replaced with something wholesome.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DXv2NOKTnMb/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🤖🔥 A Russian engineer just built a working Iron Man suit in his garage after six years of development.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXtrCxpjVsp/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 Sam Altman and OpenAI just proposed the end of the 5-day workweek.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DW6EAdYjYPK/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"GPT-6 Astra f*cking cooked Fable 5.1.","account":"sebastianhardy_","url":"https://www.instagram.com/sebastianhardy_/p/Dc_g2wOjKol/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 24 hours ago Anthropic dropped Claude Design, and people are already turning plain text prompts into polished UI, interactive prototypes, and full design systems in seconds.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXT0FNVgLWt/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 Anthropic's most powerful AI model, Claude Mythos, has reportedly been accessed by a group of unauthorized users, according to a new Bloomberg report.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXcG7QRiFep/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Chegg is becoming the clearest example of a company dismantled by generative AI.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXg8cUADUKI/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🐈 A Japanese indie developer built a Chrome extension called Cat Gatekeeper that sends a giant orange cat to sit on your screen when you scroll social media for too long.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXoT3hPgCY4/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 Anthropic just dropped Claude Opus 4.7, and it just retook the top spot as the most capable generally available AI model on the market The upgrades are built around the workflow","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXTngscAIPK/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"💸 Uber has already burned through its entire 2026 AI budget just four months into the year, and Claude Code is the reason.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXWu5M8iDyS/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 24 hours ago OpenAI dropped ChatGPT Images 2.0 on Higgsfield, and people are already coming up with crazy (NEW!) use cases.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXcAZHOiOe7/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🤯 This is getting out of control fast.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXE-Nw4jWVw/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"AI turned a Doom vs.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DXRy9vZCNW1/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"@demonflyingfox just made “Breaking Bad by Balenciaga” and you’d think a fashion house actually commissioned it.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DXYW6PRDPCm/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"“I am not buying Balenciaga.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DXYgihjjAn_/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Made by one person with AI tools, this creator's vision shows you don't need a huge studio: you need something to say.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DW_N9DOk3U2/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🏛️🧠 Aristotle didn't invent a philosophy.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DW9Q_YrDVZH/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Everyone was watching Claude replace developers.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DW69L3QgNGo/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Workers in this Indian factory aren’t just stitching clothes, they’re recording every movement they make.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DW__3KwDZsh/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🚨 The CIA just used a classified system called \"Ghost Murmur\" to find a downed American pilot in Iran by detecting his heartbeat from 40 miles away.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DW3-WEcDU8I/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Apple has officially unseated Nvidia to become the world’s largest company once again.","account":"getintoai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/getintoai/p/Da6Zt0JAcvu/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"AI just reset the ONE PIECE movie 👀🔥 It follows the full setup before the war starts.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DW1SE32DU6y/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"Tiny robots are moving in.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/reel/DXCJ5d9E22d/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"},{"title":"🏃‍♀️💨 A humanoid robot was just filmed chasing a group of wild boars through a parking lot in Warsaw.","account":"evolving.ai","url":"https://www.instagram.com/evolving.ai/p/DXGx3ZtgIKg/","at":"2026-11-17T05:17:46.825+00:00"}],"corrections":[{"said":"about stock prices for now, or if you can find anything in my Compound Finance repository that you can use, feel free. Use Codex for the daily image instead of Higgsfield and make sure it looks and feels 100% photoreal. I'm not sure we should implement this decisions piece yet. I think that's a step too far. Maybe just keep it focused on the subsectors.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine, on the news-hub data inputs","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T05:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"And on the photos you are more than welcome to take pictures of famous CEOs or common headline images that pop up as this adds a layer of trustworthiness. Figure out what you can use reliably in the small doses that are allowed, that will create a brittle fragile data pipeline that isn't hard to maintain and perhaps doesn't even require any maintenance. But it's as insightful and unique as possible.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine, on the news-hub images and data pipeline","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T05:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"It should feel like the pit stop for when you need to sharpen your decision-making, as opposed to just getting random AI news. It should feel much more and much bigger than a news feed, given what it endeavours to do and who for. I think you're going to need to bake enough variety and thoughtfulness into the use of the asset library via the instruction manual (with rotations, or I'm not sure if you have any other clever ideas), so that my page can never look like just a stream of AI-generated shapes, blocks, and Anton text. And the homepage needs to be incredibly simple to look at, with no overwhelm at all. In addition it should be completely automatic.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine, briefing the makeyourmindup.ai news-hub mockups","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T05:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Between the same covers for all of the posts and the same font for the word mark and the title, I really dislike this website compared to the current one. It's lost so much of its cinematic quality and has just faded into becoming AI slop. This looks like the most AI slop of AI slop I've ever seen in my life. I hope, dear leader, this isn't the final website. I hope this isn't what home.makeyourmindup.ai is going to end up looking like and I hope this isn't what my social channels are going to end up looking like.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine, reacting to the v5 makeyourmindup.ai front page build","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T04:39:00+00:00"},{"said":"Just build the site to the highest of standards using https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ylI3_g4gSFqW_Qm038i92vKiCDLidqeN as inspiration, then go back and make it twice as good in every way, and then push to main.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T03:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"Just approve the library when it's done and get on with everything to 100%. Re-present me with the library at the end and I can make any last-minute surgical edits if I really need to.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand) in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T03:02:00+00:00"},{"said":"Thanks for giving examples on the story motion where you said, \"Nothing acts out the story,\" but I do want to make sure that the animations fit the script. Whilst it's good to have four stable templates where reliable, I want the content engine within the session to depict what's actually being said, as opposed to only following motion templates to a story. Captions need to be much improved but can stay templated.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on the Library's motion templates","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T02:31:00+00:00"},{"said":"They are all huge failures in so many ways.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on a strip of the vertical title card, two why-2 cards and a tall scene cover, all using generic photoreal stock people (a woman on a sofa, a man on a bus) burning into colour blocks","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T01:48:00+00:00"},{"said":"Cutting off someone's head is not good and the other screen grab looks terrible.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on a carousel cover whose photo cropped a woman's head at the eyes and chin, and on a lock-screen notification cover","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T01:43:00+00:00"},{"said":"I honestly think that it might be overkill to use old-school musical artefacts in this setting. I think that we need to think much more alluring to look at, relevant, and something that everyone will relate to and recognise. I also think the image of the disc on my headshot and the way my headshot is positioned is completely stupid.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on cover mocks using a record-and-phone still as the hero card and his headshot cutout in a coral box","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T01:14:00+00:00"},{"said":"Well I think that the goal is to have aspirational templates but then leave the actual generation to the session so it generates a high-quality image that we know looks and feels like the template aspiration. I don't think we need to generate hordes and hordes of imagery to just keep on file, just in case we'll use them one day.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), answering a proposal to generate about 40 stock stills","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T01:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"I also imagine we shouldn't have generated imagery of decrepit old haunted equipment.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on a YouTube Receipt thumbnail with a generated dark mixing-desk image","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T00:59:00+00:00"},{"said":"I imagine the one, even with the shot, is some sort of encapsulating, punchy, engaging visual instead of just a Suno logo.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), on a face-led YouTube thumbnail mock with his headshot and only a Suno logo","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-26T00:58:00+00:00"},{"said":"check out all the visual covers and thumbnails on that account, for reference. There is a reason they are the current versions, after all","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), pointing at the current @makeyourmind.up Instagram covers and carousels as the reference","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T21:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"these in the screen shot have an empty feeling about them. The final card for videos should animate stunningly. Carousels should be able to generate their own images and the first card and CTA should have the wordmark on them. I also want a large variety of generated stock imagery that can be used, and check out the current carousels for where we got to which I like https://www.instagram.com/p/DfXkxIjFo_8/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&jplx=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==&avpt=MzRlODBiNWFlZA==. I imagine a lot of imagery will be generated per post, so we need to have clear guidelines and visual styles too","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the round 8 vertical video why cards (photo burning into butter and lilac blocks with the question at the top and the lower half empty)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T21:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"I dont think we need the icon separately where the wordmark exists if it has the icon inside it. Otherwise I am pretty happy with it","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the rebuilt eight archetype cards and homepage; the homepage header showed the D icon above the square wordmark that already contains it","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T20:46:00+00:00"},{"said":"I do enjoy this, it looks like an old TV which goes nicely with the records and jukeboxes","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the locked full look's YouTube banner: coral, butter, lilac and mint colour bars rising like steps on ink, with the Anton line and the D avatar over them","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T20:34:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes but there are still some unacceptable frames here. your standards need to be tighter","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the locked full look: he flagged the closing video frame (mint takeaway over an ink band with Follow for more and a small wordmark) and a tiny for Artists logo chip floating on a dark photo","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T20:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"I also resent the total loss of colour from the homepage mock too","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the makeyourmindup.ai homepage mock in the v5 look (ink ground with a single mint button)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T20:24:00+00:00"},{"said":"still looks so unprofessional and tacky like a gross powerpoint deck","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about archetype cards where one headline was split across DM Mono, Fraunces and Anton, a cream card with a white text box, and a mint card with a photo strip","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T20:22:00+00:00"},{"said":"on your questions re the burnt gradient, I imagine a carousel would be a yes but some other designs would be a no? is the creative director able to consult with you here?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), answering whether photos should burn into the colour blocks on the v5 template cards","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T19:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"these look shitty. I am worried you are approving shit outputs, how can i have a glance to make sure everything is up to scratch? I also thought these block colors were getting a burnt gradient treatment","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the Library round 6 carousel landing card and good-news item card (photo above a flat mint or butter block)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T19:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"why does all of this look misaligned","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session (makeyourmindup v5 rebrand), about the Library round 4 closing card: square wordmark, \"Follow for more\", makeyourmindup.ai","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T18:29:00+00:00"},{"said":"in the makeyourmindup session, I want every possible asset templated concretely, this includes off day pieces, and everything else. Ensure that happens thoroughly towards the start of that session","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session coordinating the AI Brain rebuild (mind/make, CTRL, makeyourmindup)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T17:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"split out CTRL and mindmake in to two separate sub sessions, do not try to manage micromanage them and ask me their questions, but your explicit job is to ensure brand coherence between CTRL (the AI Brain product), mindmake (the AI Brain services) and makeyourmindup (the AI Brain newsletter). All of these with the explicit repositioning and narrower focus in to the creative, arts, music, entertainment, media and sports industries - they all carry the same commonality of being my prior networks and experience, and a passion point for me to genuinely help with whats coming, which is greater expression of individuals, but with that comes a greater need to amplify divergence, judgement, vision, taste, creative standards - and ultimately control the IP, use it for the betterment of the creator…","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session coordinating the AI Brain rebuild (mind/make, CTRL, makeyourmindup)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T17:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"I like it but this is ridiculous how you can present this as good work.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup closing card template review)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T16:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"I like the square MAKEYOURMINDUP wordmark, but there should only be one of these wordmarks on any given artifact or page, and the headline should only appear once on any given medium (Insta bio, Substack homepage, etc etc). It doesn't need to go on every single artefact like every single close card etc","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup.ai and template Library review)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T16:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"Man, I am losing faith in the year I have spent building this fucking engine. Lets just go with \"Creativity, AI and Money, simplified.\" as the headline","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup.ai masthead heading)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T16:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"These all sound so small-minded for what is supposed to be a media channel: either small-minded or arrogant and bossy, and just lame.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup.ai heading shortlist)","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-25T15:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"I see no value in two makeyourmindup wordmarks, surely the heading should be better? Also, what from the current site should be carried over? Also plan out the UI and UX https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ylI3_g4gSFqW_Qm038i92vKiCDLidqeN","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup.ai cover mock review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T15:12:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes, except for this which does not look good in terms of alignment - we need to think about all the edge cases and repeatable usability. also where is the makeyourmindup.ai site mock you promised?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup template Library and brand book review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T14:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"s3h is great, lock v5. Once we are done rebuilding the full asset template libraries including all video production templates, I want us to figure out how content gets distributed automatically - right now I feel like there are 3 substack email blasts that go out but in reality, nobody cares enough to receive 3 deep dives a week, valuable though they are. We should figure out how to deliver an overarching newsletter with the 3 deep dives of the week, and then all the rest of the things a reader needs to know that has happened recently.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup full look v5 review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T13:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"I wanted the icon burnt in to the lettering itself not behind the lettering","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup full look v3 review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T13:21:00+00:00"},{"said":"I dont see the icon and name ghosted in t each other?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup full look v2 review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T13:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"I like it, except AI, Unpicked needs to change visually, and probably the wording too now. Also dont understand what \"PAID AT 0:30\" even means? Copy like that which is vague and smart arse needs to be banned. Also, for the icon, can we have the avatar shadowed in to the text perhaps to give it a little texture?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup full-look board review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T13:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"it all needs to work in tandem, having just one small decision at a time is not helpful to me","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup identity review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T12:59:00+00:00"},{"said":"s3g works, but I am confused where the icon goes and what the full look is?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup show art grid test)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T12:57:00+00:00"},{"said":"I like D, w0 (but i want better / more varieties of spacing), I cannot even see how Tonal Lamp is any different to the others, I like S1 and S3 equally but feel like I need to see more varieties","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup brand book v2.0 identity options)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T12:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Shown all six approved headshots side by side, Krish picked headshot-1 (dark grey studio, navy crew neck, no glasses) to replace headshot-4 (glasses, dark jacket, deep green background), which he called his least favourite, on his personal X and LinkedIn profile pictures.","about":null,"where":"claude-ai","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T08:37:37.959+00:00"},{"said":"Can we see if there are any better alternatives to the mind/make icon for makeyourmindup? and a wordmark whilst we are at it? Did we want to put sophisticated gradients on the color blocks? I also really dislike this black banner, looks so tacky. this headshot is my least favourite of them all as well","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup brand book v2.0 review)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-25T08:23:30+00:00"},{"said":"Krish picked option \"B: burn + Anton\" (a button label offered to him) from an A/B of makeyourmindup Instagram feed tiles: A locked look (photo on top, hard edge to ink), B full-bleed photo burning into ink, letter-spaced DM Mono eyebrow and Anton headline, C the same burn with a Fraunces sentence-case headline. He chose Anton over the calmer Fraunces option for feed posts, after asking to professionalise the socials like The Rundown AI without losing personality.","about":null,"where":"claude-ai","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T22:29:12.755+00:00"},{"said":"lets remove all badges like mind.the.gap from socials, and just have the wordmark left aligned with the wording at the bottom","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup feed template A/B, after picking burn + Anton)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T22:28:00+00:00"},{"said":"Yes and I wonder what you think about professionalising all the social channels as well. I don't want to lose too much personality but I also want this to come across as a sophisticated media business.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup look, sharing The Rundown AI's Instagram grid as reference)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T22:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"I wouldn't mind some burnt gradients and typography like this. That could be a nice sophistication upgrade. What do you think?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup look, sharing a The Rundown AI Instagram post as reference: photo burning to black, letter-spaced eyebrow, sentence-case headline)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T22:15:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes good - but make sure you remember how I want title animations to feel when I narrate them naturally in a sentence too. there needs to be a floor for every generated component and a floor for motion throughout too - the rest I feel like I can select from in the visual style combos if I am not mistaken","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (locking the makeyourmindup evolved look after the notes pass)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T21:29:00+00:00"},{"said":"we've lost some element of joy which i suspect went away with all the colour. I didn't want to make this completely homogenuos","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup evolved why-ladder look, notes pass after approval)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T21:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"I approve this direction, and we do not really need different colours for mon/wed/fri as such. Everything needs to be as simple to look at as possible. But the irreverant enjoyable tonality has been replaced by boring corporate sentences - just because we are upscaling in premium feel does not mean out motion animations or design or copy become boring. Also be really careful where we put the wordmark - it does not need to appear everywhere.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup evolved why-ladder frame set, cold showing)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T21:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"I want an evolution and coming of age of my existing branding, not a complete overhaul. I am largely enjoying my branding, it just needs to go through a sophistication and premium pass","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup look concept, after rejecting the overhaul mock)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T20:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"Rejected mock (\"Load-Bearing\" why-ladder look, first cold showing) was: translucent graphite panels and boxes laid over generated deadpan office stills, Fraunces serif, one citron accent, a thin progress-bar style rail, help-page and news-article screenshots as the main evidence, and no real creative work (no artists, songs, covers or performances) anywhere in the frames. Likely reading: boring = dark slabs, dimmed grey documents and no real creative work; tacky = boxes-on-photos presentation feel and UI-like chrome.","about":null,"where":"claude-ai","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T20:47:19.582+00:00"},{"said":"its amazing how you have managed to make it tacky and boring simultaneously","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (makeyourmindup new-look concept, first cold showing of the why-ladder 9:16 frame set)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T20:46:00+00:00"},{"said":"dont forget that in the makeyourmindup session, we need to ensure the engine brings the best of stories and ideas that I want to move towards, as opposed to governance, data breaches etc. I really liked the AI Music piece, it got good response the way it was broken down. we can still keep a focus on the economics of AI but in these focus sectors","about":"The AI Music piece: a Reiki master wrote a UK number two (published 11 Nov 2026)","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T20:18:12.749+00:00"},{"said":"On 24 Nov Krish picked three options I offered (my wording, his selection). Sequencing: strip calls from the backlog so it ships, then upgrade. Brand floor: replace \"bold, colourful; never muted corporate\" with \"Premium, restrained chrome in one type family and one accent per day. Colour and energy come from real creative work and motion. Never toy-like, never muted or empty, never a plain black screen.\" Leftovers: drop the opt-in prediction path, rename your.call but keep its mechanic, keep Real or Theatre restyled, replace the \"before it's obvious\" tagline with a 5 Whys line, leave old pieces as archive.","about":null,"where":"claude-ai","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T19:52:02.316+00:00"},{"said":"I honestly dont mind any of these where they have merit to make a strong visual point that is additive to my narrative point. Remember, EVERYTHING must be 10/10 fun to produce and to consume, and genuinely move the needle on people's real world understanding","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering which old-kit pieces to retire (drawn faces, felt robot, bitmoji, Anton, stickers, absurd covers)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T19:48:07.329+00:00"},{"said":"get rid of everything that suggests predictions, calls, dated, etc etc - we can keep the mon/wed/fri themes though, and just strengthen the differentiation in each theme","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T14:08:04.553+00:00"},{"said":"Yes bake in all the edge cases, the 5 Whys are designed as a mechanism the listener can follow along to, and the motion visuals can predictably complement that journey. We don't need to come to an exact conclusion by the end of the piece, but we should end up somewhere very, very insightful. This concept should be wired in to the Perplexity prompt, any claude research done, should qualify the ideas we speak about. One of the other VERY CRITICAL bits of news for you is that I am going to focus in on media, entertainment, content, arts, music and creativity for this channel moving forward - i.e focusing on how AI is impacting the new creative economy, with a positive spin. We follow creative technologies, creator technologies and anything that exists in the realm of helping individuals to e…","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T14:02:38.017+00:00"},{"said":"I also wonder if we change the signature format from Predictions/Calls, to the 5 Whys, visually walking through why something is the way it is - and that is the signature format (feel free to build on this idea). It aligns better with mind/make and makeyourmindup where the missions are to enhance the critical thinking of a leader during decision making processes. Most of all, this needs to be fun to produce, more natural, and fun to consume, as well as much, much easier to follow.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T13:51:11.86+00:00"},{"said":"we were due to give my brand look and feel an upgrade so it felt more like a premium modern news channel (i got feedback that it looks a little childish and a little like AI slop) - that goes for every part of the visual and aesthetic that touches any of this. how would you get started on this now the engines and repos are upgraded? refresh your knowledge of all the repos and the adjacent capabilities in other repos too","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-24T13:41:40.53+00:00"},{"said":"A, but just be clear that the audio waveform imagery behind it was built specifically for the AI Music piece, so that would change accordingly to the piece in a similar style. Also, I think this is one of those examples of things we can make more classy/premium","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering which title slide direction to build (two-band lockup, word by word)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T10:48:00+00:00"},{"said":"A, with Built to help you decide, and then Subscribe free at makeyourmindup.ai","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering which outro to build (intro sting at 1.5x then the tagline)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T10:48:00+00:00"},{"said":"And then this visual was really nice in how it explained additively what I was saying in the Anthropic jobs video.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, with a screenshot of the badge-grid unit chart (0%, FOLLOW.THE.MONEY, ANTHROPIC · OCT 2026)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T10:07:00+00:00"},{"said":"Just make sure that we don't lose the character.ai top half of the screen style. I really liked this for impact visually and for what it felt like watching it in terms of how it animated in. I'm sure you have already got that as a reference video and can integrate it into future videos, particularly where I deep dive into an actual platform.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T10:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"a good looking title slide, and a good looking outro are hugely important. The title slide comes in as I say the words of the title within the opening 30 seconds.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T10:02:00+00:00"},{"said":"Krish chose (multiple choice, 20 Nov): generated imagery, photoreal included, is allowed in cuts when art-directed and clearly a metaphor; only generated stand-ins for real documents, signs, places or people are refused. This replaces his earlier same-day choice of \"never\".","about":null,"where":"claude-code-web","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T09:48:25.697+00:00"},{"said":"when you say \"no AI-generated images,\" we actually do use AI to generate a lot of striking imagery that comes in and out of our pieces. We often then source real-life screenshots or I provide video/image screenshots and then they're integrated into the video to make the point a lot clearer. The AI music video is a really good example of world-class treatment of video footage and social media videos being integrated really nicely alongside generated animations.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T09:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"I'd also like to give all of the existing visuals a slight upgrade and make them classier and more consistent. I don't have any particular issue. I think we've gone to a good place with the overall brand kit but I just think there's a little bit of polish that we can do to make things just that 10% more premium to look at. This goes for: the covers, the thumbnails, the ways in which the title cards come in, the card animations, the way that photography slides in, the way that big epic moments in my script are visualised. Here are some examples of things I think are better than what we currently have. Visually it might be: the way that the burnt orange gradients, the cards, or the photos can horizontally slide in and out; the wires that connect different images to one another; the differen…","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T09:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"Krish approved the shot grammar on 20 Nov: one staging per cut (Band, Stage or Anchor) with the 3-layouts-a-minute rule retired; generated AI imagery never appears in a cut; build it and run Monday's piece on it. Answered through a multiple-choice question, so these are his choices, not typed words.","about":null,"where":"claude-code-web","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T03:39:54.877+00:00"},{"said":"They're all approved. I don't actually think these are the problem. I think how we integrate title cards and real-world images and motion animation is the issue.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T03:16:00+00:00"},{"said":"Krish asked that the home computers' engine copies never again silently run stale code after a rewrite of main's history: the recording lane failed every pass for over 24 hours after the 18 Nov history scrub and nobody was told.","about":null,"where":"claude-code-web","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-20T02:46:05.801+00:00"},{"said":"here is one which the real life visuals and my script are not bad, but the card generates over my face, the captions are awful, and the generated animations are tacky and not art directed well within the space at all","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T22:46:00+00:00"},{"said":"were just produced by two of those sessions, and they are so poor that I can't even bring myself to publish them. I refuse to. They're just the worst. Visually, motion, post-production, and everything is a zero out of ten. I'm going to need you to make sure that this can never happen again.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T22:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"No, it's awful. It's so boring. I presume the rest of the video is this boring as well, and I'm frankly fucking sick of you, and we're going to terminate this here.","about":"Tue 17 data-centres piece, long cut Gallup beat","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Tue 17 long cut's Gallup beat proof (two stat strips beside his take)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T22:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"No, the long video is awful. It's so boring. I presume the rest of the video is this boring as well, and I'm frankly fucking sick of you, and we're going to terminate this here.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long cut (Build or Buy your AI?)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T22:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"We need to eliminate the 4 million approvals like this that I'm required to make. It basically means I have to sit there for 7 hours waiting for the next stupid fucking approval to give and the engine refuses to move on even though it's just going to lead to more errors anyway.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T21:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"Whilst you're at it can you steal this motion caption and visual style? And also consider if, instead of being able to pick all three separately, it would be more stable if we just had combined templates that we know work well for all three. Instead of being able to select from many different caption styles, as well as many different motion styles, as well as many different looks","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T21:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"This palette close is fine, but what about this one in future, with built to help you decide layered on? https://claude.ai/artifact/FnDVNoCk1CqxGKTHRYENKH","about":"The tall close: the intro sting with \"Built to help you decide\" layered on, as a future end card","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering which wins between the palette close and the plain-black guard","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T20:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"Keep shadow only","about":"Art-directed captions over a bright photo: shadow only, no scrim","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering whether captions over the white bill on the steak beat need a scrim","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T20:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"Also, this could be the tall video closing card (with Built to help you decide layered on in a good looking way)","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T20:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"LOOKS GOOD GO GO GO","about":"The Fri 20 Nov short proof","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, replying to the Fri 20 Nov short's 8 s proof (slam words over the bill page, title over the sofa and closet plates, no music bars)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T15:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"As I think I've told you 400,000 times, the word mark needs to be aligned with the title.","about":"Tue 17 data-centres piece, the title's wordmark placement","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Tue 17 long cut's title proof","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T15:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes change for all moving forward - but bear in mind that the audio waveform visual behind it was made for a piece about AI music specifically. In the future, the engine needs to find its own visual that matches the piece.","about":"The house title card's background (an audio waveform from the AI music piece) and its dark bands","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (Fri 20 Nov production session), answering whether to change the house title card","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T15:19:00+00:00"},{"said":"give me a title card failure report, as I expect the title card to enter as I am talking, and the title of the piece is woven in to my script at the start. This is a good example of what actually was a good build for the title card.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (Wed 18 production session, relayed with the Wed 11 AI MUSIC title as the example)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T13:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"canva drafts are always shitty, forget about canva","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, after the rejected Canva Start here Story frame","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-19T12:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"That's such a shitty, boring prediction. Who cares? Who gives a fuck? This has already happened like thousands of times. I hate this prediction format. I think we just scrap it.","about":"The dated prediction at the end of the Fri 20 Nov article (and the prediction format itself)","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (Fri 20 Nov production session), answering which prediction the article should carry","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T12:41:00+00:00"},{"said":"It looks terrible and boring and off-brand, and components are cramped, and it doesn't have anything enjoyable about it. It feels like you've not read any of my engines, and you've just met me for the first time and produced some piece of shit that you would produce for anyone.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, on the Instagram 'Start here' highlight Story frame draft (Canva copy of the story-action template)","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-19T12:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"No, these are not funny. and They're too long.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine (meme skill, GTA 6 boss captions); time approximate","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T12:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"This is a good example of what actually was a good build for the title card.","about":"A full-frame centred title lockup on angled bands with the stacked wordmark beneath (the AI music title)","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, sharing a screenshot of the \"AI MUSIC or HUMAN MUSIC?\" title frame","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T11:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"Nothing is aligned, though. It should animate in and all be one feature, aligned properly. not a wordmark temporarily in the bottom right, disconnected from the title.","about":"The title card and the wordmark must be one aligned unit that animates in together","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 title-card frames (long and short)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T11:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"oh my god STOP ASKING ME TO APPROVE EVERYTHING, NO OTHER SESSION IS DOING THIS, JUST FUCKING GET THIS DONE","about":"Sessions keep asking him to approve engine versions and proofs","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, after the Wed 18 wide-layout stills and an engine approval request","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T10:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"These Perplexity prompts are not deep enough at all. They're so vague.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the 10 whys Perplexity prompts for Wed 25 Nov, Fri 27 Nov and the vibe coding idea","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T10:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"monthly live session + a teardown for annual, and then for founding members all brain modules are free, plus a monthly check in with Krish to unpick your biggest AI bottlenecks","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/makeyourmindup, setting the paid Substack perks per plan","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-19T10:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"No, the \"crazy\" looks tacky. The checkout lady is just scanning the same box over and over and over again, and it doesn't land that we're talking about AI here. It looks like a supermarket. Components are cut off. Somehow, this has gone 10 times worse. Can you go back to pulling the content engine repo fresh and deciding on the fastest way to get from where we are now to a world-class production, given we already have loads of assets as well as loads of motion templates?","about":"Generated comic scenes, the CRAZY slam and clipped stamps made the long cut worse","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long cut's 15/10 rebuild reel","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T10:15:00+00:00"},{"said":"This is a really good idea. That's a good headline and I really want to draw into making it simple to understand what AI is actually doing to education. There was a lot of uproar when the Department of Education was dissolved in America and there are rumbling theories that educational institutions are screwed. What's actually true and where will education end up?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine, about the \"$75K for an AI school day\" carousel approved for Tue 24 Nov","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T10:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"Switch the monthly and annual perks around? Annual members should get a more consultative piece of work delivered to them, monthly should get the automated modules they can buy","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/makeyourmindup, correcting the proposed paid Substack perks per plan","repository":"krishanraja/makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-19T10:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Would be funny to have visuals of skeletons coming out of closets and money back down the back of couches in the right moments.","about":"Will your AI auditor find your missing money, or the skeletons in your closet?","where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-fri-produce-mwncy0wc","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T09:38:29.772+00:00"},{"said":"It's a boring topic, and you have accompanied it with boring visuals. I said at the start, that when the topic is dull but important, the visuals need to be 15/10 in terms of captivating","about":"A dull but important topic needs 15/10 captivating visuals","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long cut's visuals","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T09:33:00+00:00"},{"said":"It's a 5/10, it just pulses 3 logos, it doesnt really move with what I am saying much. I hope the rest of the long video is not that motionless? Nothing technically wrong with it, it's just not doing much.","about":"Long cut motion: graphics must move with what he says, not pulse three logos","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long hook proof v5","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T09:31:00+00:00"},{"said":"and its both - makeyourmindup should always have good humour","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, answering whether the Substack welcome email is the publication's surface or outbound email","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-19T09:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"Why the fuck are you allowed to just make things much worse and not even bother looking at screenshots like this, knowing that it's clearly fucked up?","about":"Proof v10 sent with visible faults","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, after proof v10 of the habits short","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T08:08:00+00:00"},{"said":"The intro looks better as a hook but the logos are either invisible or they're completely out of proportion.","about":"Logos on a dark card: every mark visible and the same visual weight","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long hook proof v3 (Fin logo dark on dark, Salesforce cloud oversized)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T08:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"It has seriously regressed. The subtitles are now in the wrong place and there's loads of black space underneath. I already told you I don't want a plain black screen anywhere.","about":"Proof v10 of the habits short: caption placement and black space","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on proof v10 of the habits short (the updated caption engine)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T08:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"I also think that, considering that's the first few seconds of the video, it's not much of a hook. It looks quite dull for the first 3 seconds.","about":"Wed 18 long cut: a static logo card in the first 3 seconds is not a hook","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long cut's hook proof","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T03:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"On your long proof I think that my head needs to be in the bottom right. It doesn't look right as it is. Particularly if the subtitles are going to be not centralised, then something needs to be in the bottom right.","about":"Wed 18 long cut: his head belongs in the bottom right on the proof beats, opposite the left-aligned captions","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 long cut's hook proof","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-19T02:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"\"Dont cut the top of my head off\" should not really need a reference image, should it?","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T22:11:36+00:00"},{"said":"But this treatment is not good. Can't cut my head off and also ruin the visual above","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T22:11:36+00:00"},{"said":"either ai music or character.ai is fine - both are good for different reasons. DELETE THOSE FRAMES FOREVER. you need to rebuild everywhere it was to be 10X better using those two new references","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T22:11:36+00:00"},{"said":"this font is crappy, I have given this feedback before - why would it still keep popping up in carousels?","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T22:11:36+00:00"},{"said":"finish round two but honestly i dont get what it is a reference of, and why a visual pass plus obvious rules arent a better option than measuring it against one frame of an old video","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T20:57:46+00:00"},{"said":"make this a carousel, lets map out the story of the cards","about":null,"where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-tue-post-mwmkiqet","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T20:22:47.093+00:00"},{"said":"the visual for the cover needs to be way more interesting than a screen shot of a website","about":"Receipt cover visual for the Tue 17 Nov habits short","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the habits short's Receipt cover options","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T20:13:00+00:00"},{"said":"Subtle texture","about":"The moving texture on the screens' black ground","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the moving texture for the black screen grounds of the habits voiceover short","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T19:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"we have two concurrent visual styles trying to say the same thing over one another? why?","about":"Tue 17 short: a drawn data-centre block over photographs of data halls, pylons and polling stations says the same thing twice","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Tue 17 short's data-centre block drawn over photo backdrops","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T19:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"Looks good but I hope we spend no longer on a visual as dull as a report than this clip. Also could have some sort of nice moving texture on the black background?","about":"How long a report-page visual may stay on screen, and the plain black ground behind screens","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on proof v4 (the IBM page beats) of the habits voiceover short","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T19:37:00+00:00"},{"said":"But this treatment is not good. Can't cut my head off and also ruin the visual above","about":"Wed 18 build-or-buy short: the split beat crops the top of his head and squeezes the crocodile stand-off still into a letterboxed strip","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Wed 18 short's hook proof (the SPLIT beat: a still held above his take)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T19:35:00+00:00"},{"said":"this visual is a bit small, and also \"Where does AI get built when the residents of town say no to data centers?\" should be seamlessly made the title with epic hero title treatment as I am saying that line. everything else is good","about":"Tue 17 short: the 41 local votes graphic is too small; the opening question should become an epic hero title as he says it","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Tue 17 short's 41 local votes graphic and its opening line","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T18:46:00+00:00"},{"said":"The crocodile scene just keeps pulsing as a still. Surely that's going to be turned into a moving video with Codex, right? Music seems good, and it is a mad bag of cats","about":"The Wed 18 short's hook proof: a generated still that pulses, and its music","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (cloud), on the Wed 18 short's hook proof and its Mind Bender bed","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T18:15:00+00:00"},{"said":"the word VOID is in the same font and style as the captions which looks misleading visually, but the rest looks good","about":"The VOID slam on b10b set in the captions' type","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on proof v2 of the habits voiceover short","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T17:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"Aspire, but turn the volume down 15%. I have some issues with the subtitles. They are really jolty, and each word moving from left to right is really hard to look at and stressful. We can't have each new word appear somewhere else on the screen, and we need the previous word to stick around for a tiny bit longer. I think you're going to need to get creative here or use a different caption set because this one feels really stressful. I also don't think you're really being thoughtful about when the full screen cuts over my face and when my face comes back in, and making actual use of the full screen when it isn't my face (because often I'm seeing it cut away to a black screen with not much on it but subtitles). Just get Codex to generate the scenes. Not Higgsfield.","about":"Art-directed captions and face/full-screen cutaways on the Tue 17 short","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (post-production of the Tue 17 data-centres piece)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T17:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"I like it - it seems fast, can we just slow it all down 10%, but yeah I like this","about":"The proof of the habits voiceover short at 1.2x","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the proof of the habits voiceover short","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T17:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"WHERE IS THIS IMAGE BEING USED TO REFERENCE WHEN PRODUCING NEW CONTENT AND WHY? WE NEED TO PURGE IT FROM THE EXISTENCE OF HUMANITY AND FIND BETTER REFERENCES","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine, about the three-frame Thu 5 Nov face-with-proof screenshot","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T17:30:06+00:00"},{"said":"why are you STILL USING THIS AS A REFERENCE I HAVE ASKED YOU SO MANY TIMES TO DELETE THIS FROM ALL EXISTENCE THIS IS THE WORST EXAMPLE OF ANY CONTENT EVERY MADE","about":"The design lock's face-with-proof key frames were frames of his rejected Thu 5 Nov take","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine (cloud), on the face-with-proof design-lock key frames cut from the Thu 5 Nov No Spending take","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T17:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"people trying to defy new technologies instead of embracing them for themselves and being accountable for what they do - such as people trying to navigate with a paper map in a car with satnav, or trying to outrun a car","about":null,"where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-tue-produce-mwmbf7n7","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T16:08:06.259+00:00"},{"said":"people trying to defy new technologies instead of embracing them for themselves and being accountable for what they do - such as people trying to navigate with a paper map in a car with satnav, or trying to outrun a car","about":"Points the habits voiceover short must make visually, added to its production plan","where":"comment on the Tuesday 17 Nov publish board in Control Centre (desk-tue-produce), on the production plan","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T16:08:06+00:00"},{"said":"A really clear visual about being enticed to upgrade with free credits, but the small print actually reducing your overall monthly limits to the tool","about":"Where does AI get built when towns say no?","where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-tue-produce-mwmavlz0","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T15:52:51.708+00:00"},{"said":"1 get rid of that - i have abandoned the prediction format, it feels lame. you need to start acting like a 200K head of growth for makeyourmindup not an intern","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup (Remote Control, worker), replying to a list where item 1 was content-engine's publish checks and house rules still forcing a dated prediction into every article","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-18T15:05:00+00:00"},{"said":"extend the humour ruling to messages and forms too, I want to express personality, enthusiasm, hilarity, fun and a epic positive energy in the first impression, but not in a fake way - very me, and very positive about my mission of helping people to not feel left behind, and make it easy to grasp complex things","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/ai-harness (skill curator for the Make Your Mind Up growth push)","repository":"krishanraja/ai-harness","at":"2026-11-18T13:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"i preferred the amount of workers and how they were roughly split out in this one - taste, judgement, vision, standards, inspiration, divergent thinker consultant, voice checker. Librarian is just one part of an AI brain - it's really the proactive chief of staff that has a librarian, auditor, analyst, trend spotter, inspiration-house, file archives as well as content archives and all the above. It's been dumbed down way too much now as has have all the floors above it. we need to find something closer to the source post I sent you","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T11:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"it's gotten too simple now in terms of words","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T10:58:00+00:00"},{"said":"The screenshots hide behind my head a little bit too much here.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the face-led cover examples (real cutout plus post figure)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T07:35:00+00:00"},{"said":"The last card of the carousel should always have the \"Make Your Mind Up\" word mark centred under the \"Follow for more\" text, as opposed to the word mark in the bottom-right corner and an amateur call to action.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the close card of the ads and midterms carousels","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T07:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"The cover image of the carousel should always be more sensational. Have a real-life person in them, or a sensational real-life visual screenshot, or a really really well put together generated image.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on new carousel cover scenes","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T06:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"I think with the data centres one, it could be \"Where could AI live now?\" because if that hasn't happened yet. For both covers the image needs to be more absurd, hilarious, and creative. In the ads one the robot should be visibly getting sold to, left, right, and centre. In fact this should be a human. The robot shouldn't be in this one. This should be a photorealistic image of ChatGPT, open with sponsored links and suggestions everywhere. The text in all the cards that are not the cover card is not acceptable in terms of the font treatment. I agree that they don't need to look the same as the intro and outro but the font and look are substandard.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the ads and midterms carousels in the house look","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T06:36:00+00:00"},{"said":"in this one the cover was the most underwhelming, the rest of the cards were good - https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1feD3BsGArlyUQTK_TTtNf8EqgV-c3qA6?usp=drive_link","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Erdős carousel (\"AI broke an 80-year-old maths belief.\")","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T02:14:00+00:00"},{"said":"in these two, the cover image was great but the rest of the cards were not - https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1h04Vm_T4lw-91u-lWvDocCAk_pwS5jyO?usp=drive_link","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, sending two past carousel covers (\"Your AI thinks it's the best. Guess who told it.\" and \"Anthropic's AI broke Git.\") as the cover style for all carousels","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T02:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"right aligned to the video. ALso on the carousels, they need to stick to the style of the one we did on anthropic & git. in terms of the cover page. We need real world images where possible. the carousel templates need to be 100X better in all ways","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the Hank meme (wordmark placement) and the midterms carousel draft","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T02:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Never first person, always \"When you realize...\" or \"POV: you realize...\". And the wordmark always goes right aligned at the bottom on memes","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on two meme template reskins for Thu 19 Nov (Hank slowly realises, Pigeon doctor)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T01:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"I want this experiment skill to literally be capable of going nuts - putting me on space, having me turn in to sam altman randomly, absolutely nuts stuff that has ZERO limits. make it so","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T01:31:00+00:00"},{"said":"These two","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/krish-clone, with a screenshot circling loft A as generated and still 1 with in-between broader shoulders","repository":"krishanraja/krish-clone","at":"2026-11-18T00:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"I also prefer A in this palette.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/krish-clone, on four loft-window generated headshots of himself (A to D)","repository":"krishanraja/krish-clone","at":"2026-11-18T00:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"One and two are loft B. Three is somewhere in the middle of two shoulders.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/krish-clone, on broader-shoulder edits of generated headshots (loft B, loft D, still 1)","repository":"krishanraja/krish-clone","at":"2026-11-18T00:35:00+00:00"},{"said":"I have broader shoulders than that. Image 1 could also benefit from broader shoulders.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/krish-clone, on four generated loft-window headshots of himself and approved headshot 1","repository":"krishanraja/krish-clone","at":"2026-11-18T00:30:30+00:00"},{"said":"I'll go from left to right and top to bottom. 1. Image 1 looks good and could pass for me. 2. Image 2: my chin is too small. 3. Image 3 is good and could pass for me. 4. Image 4 is good and could pass for me. 5. Image 5 looks nothing like me. 6. Image 6 is good and could pass for me.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/krish-clone, judging six colour-corrected generated headshots of himself for face-led covers","repository":"krishanraja/krish-clone","at":"2026-11-18T00:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"It's also the vocabulary she uses, as opposed to even your latest hospital care script, which used words like \"dearest,\" which I would never say in a million years.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T00:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"the first one is better.","about":"Tue 17 data-centres short: podcast (Two-line scroll) preferred over karaoke","where":"Claude Code post-production session on the Tue 17 data-centres short, shown the same 8 seconds in podcast (Two-line scroll) and karaoke; his pick was podcast; quoted verbatim in the repair brief; date known, time of day not","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"I have some issues with the subtitles. They are really jolty, and each word moving from left to right is really hard to look at and stressful. We can't have each new word appear somewhere else on the screen, and we need the previous word to stick around for a tiny bit longer. I think you're going to need to get creative here or use a different caption set because this one feels really stressful.","about":"Tue 17 data-centres short, art-directed captions on one-word pages","where":"Claude Code post-production session on the Tue 17 data-centres short (art-directed captions), quoted verbatim in the repair brief to this session; date known, time of day not","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"this looks god to me. can you ensure there is a carousel skill that exists that hardens all the prior carousel failures too (lack of clear narrative from card to card able to be understood in isolation with zero context, poor imagery, cover not eye grabbing at all, etc etc), and a meme skill too (we dont have standards for meme videos yet but we have just begun to upgrade this).","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the cover palette approval pack (face-free Receipt skins, face-led real and generated covers, headshot bank, channel and rotation rules)","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T23:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"the fact that my shoulders cut off is unacceptable. also can we experiment with imagery (real life or generated) that the covers would be generating for a specific post, being incorporated with my headshot? run examples of old posts so we can see what they look like - keep it classy","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, on the round-four face-led tall cover options (cutout headshots whose shoulders ended at the photo's edge), with four reference YouTube thumbnails attached","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T22:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"To be honest with you, I don't do dated-and-scored make-your-mind-up pieces because it felt quite tacky and gimmicky. I don't really have the clout such that my opinion can hold up in official scores.. Lets get rid of that from the cover page makeyourmindup repo and all documentation","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-17T19:15:00+00:00"},{"said":"We need to flesh this out and lightly educate the reader or the viewer on the fact that AI works well in retrospect. It would be good if we could find some more entertaining or funny examples of things that AI has corrected, maybe from Reddit or something. I want this one to be an acid test of how we can make a really boring topic really fun, entertaining, and funny. The main central theme and idea of this is singular: that you might want to set it to work as an auditor that picks up tiny details from your business's past. But be careful what you wish for, and if you have any skeletons in the closet, then it might dig those up too.","about":"Axiom rebuilt a 15,000-page proof in 24 days with an agent swarm. The interesting part is the bug it found.","where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-fri-story-mwl0ndfx","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T18:18:45.069+00:00"},{"said":"scripts should show for carousels and memes as well - there is copy on every single post","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T16:37:00+00:00"},{"said":"Just say \"Claude uses a ton of other companies software internally, when we all know its the business most other businesses build their software on.\" as the intro sentence","about":"Wed 18 90-second cut: his own intro sentence","where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:58:00+00:00"},{"said":"I don't understand what \"over a shed of computers\" means, and I don't understand what \"could its power end up on your bill\" means. The word \"shed\" is not common knowledge, not even to me, let alone my audience. Did you use the word \"shed\" because you think it's understandable by an 8-year-old? Because now it's understandable by nobody.","about":"\"Shed\" as a stand-in for data centre in the Tue 17 scripts","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:50:00+00:00"},{"said":"When we say \"Anthropic, which makes Claude, pays other companies for customer service\", that does not introduce the piece properly. The first paragraph is just not hooking enough on the 90 sec script","about":"Wed 18 90-second cut: opening line not hooking","where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:38:00+00:00"},{"said":"the one story rule is only really for the 90 second video. the long cut can have more to it, but it needs to be coherently explained, always - or used as further evidence, or a counterpoint. Remember - always needs to be fun to produce and consume. 75 word script is insanely short. the AI music short is about the right amount of words, maybe just less","about":"Script length and the one-story rule (Tue 17 data centres)","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"whenever I press approve script, the new board state should be waiting for me to confirm the videos are in the Inbox, at which point it will fetch the name of the video(s) and integrate them in the piece on the board so the next post production prompt does a completely accurate job, with all the research, motion styles etc being in one place and decided as well, the post production should always be one shot - and can decide where to bring in logos, real visuals, social posts, screen shots, motion design, cinematic generation, my face etc etc.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"Relayed by another Claude session (session_01JRhKytFcFVtUWn8teqtkUB), Krish on 17 Nov 2026 about the Content board: \"at no point does a voiceover short give me the same controls as a mon/wed/fri piece in terms of the motion, captions etc etc. why not?\" He wants off-day video posts (voiceover shorts) to offer the same look, motion style and caption picks as the series pieces, on every day.","about":null,"where":"claude-code-web","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:08:21.955+00:00"},{"said":"well ultimately all this feedback applies to all relevant days, i told you i do not want one off fixes but system upgrades","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T15:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"at no point does a voiceover short give me the same controls as a mon/wed/fri piece in terms of the motion, captions etc etc. why not?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T14:58:00+00:00"},{"said":"presumably when it gets to this stage and the files are in teleprompter, the next action presumes I have recorded the video and put it in the inbox, and thats what the next button's prompt is there to do in Claude?Also can you stop having my Claude production prompt buttons open up a new browser window? Just copy to clipboard is enough for all such buttons","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T14:53:00+00:00"},{"said":"cut curative, one story only is critical for 90 second pieces","about":"Wed 18 90-second cut: one story only","where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T13:24:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes to the face plan","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering a proposal: face-led covers (large cutout headshot, no circle) on his personal accounts (TikTok, X, LinkedIn, Threads, Substack Notes), a Receipt vs face A/B test on YouTube, Receipt kept on Instagram, Facebook and Substack","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T12:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Fuck me, I am now northern, gay and posh","about":"Krish v2 voice on eleven_v3, paragraph takes: the accent drifted from his approved opening","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:57:00+00:00"},{"said":"yes, 15% is right, go ahead - ensure the krish-clone repo and the other two sessions know that this is the best choice thus far in terms of voice ID and your usage of it","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, approving ElevenLabs \"Krish v2\" (EWMCMyM8o9ZcYCijk7nx) on eleven_v3 with audio tags, the take sped up 15%, as his narration voice","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:46:00+00:00"},{"said":"v2, take A - but needs to speak 15% faster","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, picking among ElevenLabs takes of his remixed voices; v2 is \"Krish v2\" (EWMCMyM8o9ZcYCijk7nx) on eleven_v3","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:45:00+00:00"},{"said":"EWMCMyM8o9ZcYCijk7nx and zBnYxhtZxkcWwYsi497n are new variations I like, try these","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, naming two ElevenLabs Voice Remix variations of his Krish Remix voice (\"Krish v2\" and \"Krish v1\") made for softer, glottal T's","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:40:00+00:00"},{"said":"Is the kind of intro that matches with the AI music video I did, where \"build or buy your tools in an AI world?\" would end up being the title, treated visually as such, seamlessly flowing out of the captions and back in to them again. And then the entire piece should acknowledge the millions of vibe coded tools out there, and the ability for you to install Claude packs that everyone sells on LinkedIn. These are all ways in which people are getting sold: how to use AI right now. I think that this piece needs to cover the full spectrum. The 90-second script needs to be hilarious and relatable to all, and make the viewer want to see the full 5-minute video, which is something we've not done before.","about":"Wed 18 build or buy: his intro, title treatment, spectrum and 90-second cut","where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:30:00+00:00"},{"said":"take 2 is good - how can we surgically improve my voice for future use","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, judging ElevenLabs takes of his Krish Remix voice (FOupAntbAMhJ9n9Q4dfC) on eleven_v3 with delivery tags [excited] [casual] [playful] [conversational]","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:28:00+00:00"},{"said":"\"\"ChatGPT wrote it.\" Mate, no one cares.\" is weak - the quote doesnt sound like a quote when read out like that. Usually, what happens is people just say, \"AI isn't very good, is it?\" and the \"Mate, no one cares \" should be something more like \"That's the claim of someone who is going to blame their tools for their work, which hasn't ever gone down well in the past\"","about":"Tue habits voiceover script: a quoted line that doesn't read as a quote when voiced","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:25:00+00:00"},{"said":"I don't enunciate my T's as much as this, and I am a bit more animated - can you help me create a voice in eleven labs I am happy with? perhaps in a separate session?","about":"Krish Remix voice on eleven_v3: too crisp on T's, not animated enough","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:21:00+00:00"},{"said":"Now they just sound like completely different humans entirely. Remember that what we're working off of was trained on all of my voice inputs.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, judging three ElevenLabs voice-design previews built from a text description instead of his trained voice","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"v3 sounds right, re-voice the full script on that","about":"Krish Remix voice (FOupAntbAMhJ9n9Q4dfC): eleven_v3 sounds like it; eleven_v4 did not","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:16:00+00:00"},{"said":"A younger voice, more casual vocab - \"you can't sack an AI, so who gets the boot? probably you\". We should also really touch upon the fact that humans are blaming AI for errors. Just like we don't put cars on trial when road accidents happen, the only way humans are going to not be replaced by AI is if they become even more accountable and take ownership of AI's mistakes. We really need to drill this point home and then go into the three habits virality piece. We need to make this really share-worthy and sensational. Can you use voice FOupAntbAMhJ9n9Q4dfC","about":"Tue 17 Nov habits voiceover short script and voice","where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T10:12:00+00:00"},{"said":"Let's make this one more provocative. Given it's a voiceover, Get ElevenLabs to generate a some voice options for me first. Write it like that and have it be a 90-second only. Remember that for voiceovers without video, the visuals really need to do 10x of the heavy lifting.","about":null,"where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-tue-post-mwkisry7","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T09:59:04.063+00:00"},{"said":"remember - every script should be great fun to deliver, and to consume, like the AI Music one was","about":null,"where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T09:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"Make this 11 out of 10: fun, tongue-in-cheek, and surprisingly informative for any layperson.","about":"OpenAI pledges to pay for data center power after election highlights AI concerns","where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-tue-story-mwkin9j7","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T09:54:46.915+00:00"},{"said":"these scripts are awful - they make zero sense and have regressed a huge amount. I want the quality of the AI Music or Human Music script (what I actually said on film) to be the floor for all future scripts tonally","about":"Wed 18 Nov scripts (build versus buy), approved then rejected on tone","where":"Claude Code cloud session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T09:10:00+00:00"},{"said":"They don't open sincerely, casually, sound like my voice at all. They open with a blanket statement which is one of the worst AI email patterns on earth. We should also give them my krishraja.com link because that credentializes me incredibly fast. Are you using the depth of knowledge about my voice?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, reviewing 10 drafted Substack recommendation-swap pitches to other newsletter writers","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-17T09:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"We need a lot more relatable build-versus-buy decisions and stories of engineers going wild and commercial leaders with their eyes bigger than their stomachs on building stuff. We also need examples of software that just charge through the roof. This piece needs to be hilarious and tongue-in-cheek. In terms of the video but in terms of the article, it needs to be enterprise-grade and really show the minutia in the economics of build versus buy (in a way that even an 8-year-old could understand it) and enterprise-level visuals as well. I think you might need to give me a prompt for Perplexity so I can bring you back some deeper research here.","about":"The labs writing everyone's code still run Salesforce","where":"publish board in Control Centre, his notes for Claude, 2026-11-16 comments/desk-wed-board-mwkds5uw","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-17T07:38:37.352+00:00"},{"said":"A style may bring in its own colours and theming as long as it doesn't end up looking like a clown's apron. I want to experiment with variety, colour, and visual styles. We're in the experimental stage of content creation here, as opposed to being obsessive about brand guidelines. We've got barely any audience so whatever we need to do to know what works is the most important thing.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, answering whether video styles and their covers may leave the ink, cream and mint palette","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T15:36:00+00:00"},{"said":"Something's gone wrong in where you're looking and how you're looking because there should be millions of good news stories. What about Reddit, YouTube, or LinkedIn? Given that it's business leaders, we might want some successful business stories as well. In fact successful business stories might be really good.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, about the Saturday good news finding only four stories","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T15:24:00+00:00"},{"said":"Throw a few emojis in there, like laughing emojis and things like that.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, reviewing redrafted wave 2 comments on other people's posts (X, Substack Notes, Instagram)","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-16T15:20:00+00:00"},{"said":"They're too pristine, not sharp enough, and not rough and human enough. Have you got access to my voice profile and my humour profile?","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup, reviewing wave 2 of drafted comments on other people's posts (X, Substack Notes, Instagram)","repository":"krishanraja/growth-makeyourmindup","at":"2026-11-16T15:00:00+00:00"},{"said":"Good news stories can come from the Instagram inspo as well. There's absolutely tonnes in there. We would just need to pick the right ones if the good news was on a specific theme.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, about the Saturday good news","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T13:55:00+00:00"},{"said":"Make sure on mobile I can click on the image and expand it. I'd also make it easier to slide up and slide down drawers. Right now I have to click outside of the drawer to slide it back down, which is not the easiest. Make that easier.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, about Control Centre's piece sheet on his phone","repository":"krishanraja/control-center","at":"2026-11-16T13:41:00+00:00"},{"said":"This is more or less the only screenshot I've ever shared. I told you how much I hate it in every way possible. Please don't tell me this is going on the board as an example or a gold standard template that we could use in future projects.","about":null,"where":"Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine, of the style-lab still from the Thu 5 Nov No Spending take","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T12:48:00+00:00"},{"said":"- \"nope, cannot see it\"","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar.","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"- \"Stop the Control Center and credits work, and don't change any more MCP or Claude settings.","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Don't post, send or change anything else.\"","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Don't change any MCP or Claude settings.\"","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"\"Don't post, send or change anything else.\"","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Never use the plugin’s long-running server.","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"},{"said":"Stop the Control Center and credits work, and don’t change any more MCP or Claude settings.","about":null,"where":"a Claude Code session in krishanraja/content-engine","repository":"krishanraja/content-engine","at":"2026-11-16T11:34:27+00:00"}],"hindsight":[{"piece_id":"7083d6ad-419e-4fdc-9aba-f3be7f3f3a23","narrative":8,"production":8,"note":"This was very clear and thought-provoking. The production quality was really good and the script was clear as well.","at":"2026-11-07T16:10:22.762+00:00"},{"piece_id":"b63d2507-dbb4-449d-bce4-f21e859ee2ad","narrative":7,"production":5,"note":"The opening doesn't have enough of a hook. The animations get cut off. They're not full screen, specifically when there's the hand holding the phone. The screenshots are just not really clear enough in terms of being able to make a clear point. As I was watching the videos I couldn't really understand or see properly what the screenshots even were or what was happening there. Overall clarity of production was a bit lower.","at":"2026-11-07T16:08:57.651+00:00"},{"piece_id":"9a0c97af-f0d6-4d12-a7ce-773c622d4b67","narrative":6,"production":8,"note":"I think this was one of the strongest in terms of the animation style of the job badges etc","at":"2026-11-07T16:06:48.594+00:00"}],"unread":[]},"cues":{"future_pieces":[{"id":"3aa537c7-bc4e-41d1-a27e-a1496162a1d5","subject_ref":"829df1ea-8fca-4661-bd90-39cf3566e7d4","subject":"Who pays for a free AI picture: you, or the brand in the progress bar? ChatGPT starts showing ads while your image draws, and only to people who do not pay.","said":"I am passionate about the message which is if you are not paying, you are the product. But I think this needs a bit more substance as to how this intersects with content IP in terms of a monetization play. I think we need to really clearly visualize and unpick where the money goes and if OpenAI are using ads too, to be able to avoid a more intricate system where they pay for the content being used to generate images","said_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:43.078+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"86295389-e804-4d81-a265-96bae74fe77c","subject_ref":"385a5da8-2cae-41ec-8fb6-2e328920664c","subject":"Inspiration card \"09 Reading is free. Sending needs a yes.\" (unknown)","said":"It's just good general advice for other topics that are more interesting than this.","said_at":"2026-10-24T06:17:11.161+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"7192a8ee-628c-469a-9a90-9b41e9ce5139","subject_ref":"3e5f0e5a-0bf6-4bd9-b6b5-a207f33dc364","subject":"Nvidia's biggest customer is building its way out: Microsoft will run most of its own AI on its own chip, so who keeps the margin, and does anyone's AI bill go","said":"Move number 3 to Wednesday's queue for later.","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:23.604+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"68c03220-20a4-4795-930c-e8880cef7db8","subject_ref":"5b726fc3-ac63-4607-9293-3257b4ecc75c","subject":"Turn the usual fear around: AI was meant to make writing worthless, and the engineers are saying the opposite. Kaseya's technology chief says the new code is","said":"number 4 absolutely needs to be saved for the future.","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:28.155+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"93503b71-1dd8-4391-8343-2713f674564c","subject_ref":"2b582f5a-52fb-49a3-8502-0e9bd914f772","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube 7olCmqWw9Wk\" by Ksh2.0 (youtube)","said":"We should reskin this as a hilarious video meme for when your AI talks to your customer's AI.","said_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:16.328+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"d3a3d8bd-832d-4ced-8ab1-d4bdcc475636","subject_ref":"87a82f7f-6411-41c9-92b1-a52c4f3e4f8a","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DfAY9PWFuEX 01\" (instagram)","said":"Just a positive ray of sunshine. I'd love to post a week out that is just amazing, with positive things being done with AI.","said_at":"2026-10-27T19:50:33.092+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"7107fa22-7657-4034-b27c-1c1a4ef64739","subject_ref":"7f43c6b5-a468-40f3-ad66-c988cdc16072","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DePHDr jRed\" by georgia_la (instagram)","said":"I'm going to be doing a clean shot of me explaining something about AI and how to build your brain, for example, or just a quick 1-2-3 step. This would be a nice candid way of doing it with nice lighting, a good-quality shot, and nice subtitle builds as well as a really good thumbnail like this one.  https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WVmopXVzY0NOKUuQQIH0tubIa1hwLHU_/view?usp=drivesdk","said_at":"2026-10-28T22:57:28.648+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"29efa199-7c5a-4d58-8621-7d7f2d4ba0fb","subject_ref":"36886e0b-4b32-473b-be72-b0aef31fccef","subject":"AI is already inside the songs people have on repeat, hidden in the credits. Movin' To The Sun started as a Suno demo, was rebuilt by HUGEL with a new Ultra","said":"Story, run it as under.the.hood","said_at":"2026-10-31T16:37:17.832+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"707c0eb7-6ea9-41a7-8642-22909fc84212","subject_ref":"2162c904-b0ff-452b-81aa-b8cfd7ec1909","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DeypYeWN5hL\" by buildwithomkar (instagram)","said":"This is good for both production and content. We should do a short that just completely reskins and reuses the content and production of this.","said_at":"2026-11-02T14:08:53.873+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"cd817c71-1641-4550-8992-84ef83a49449","subject_ref":"da3cacd1-b038-4827-bd22-1d4d9be07889","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DeR9G-JNf-8\" by buildwithomkar (instagram)","said":"Let's literally copy the content and production for this and just reskin it ASAP.","said_at":"2026-11-02T23:19:21.327+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"99a5d6d1-1031-4ccc-9d9d-d81d4ad20d71","subject_ref":"d16fe9ff-413c-47c4-ac53-c89e40d28489","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube tJwqPQvgQkk\" by Geek Creative Agency (youtube)","said":"Lets make a hilarious meme. Reskin this video with the text \"POV: your AI agent when you forget to teach it anything that matters to you\"","said_at":"2026-11-03T10:11:01.742+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"82b9ef23-dfdb-40c6-9113-6e22b9097642","subject_ref":"50368dee-0a10-4452-a79a-0607d4f2e278","subject":"Inspiration card \"screenshot-20261105-060348\" (linkedin)","said":"We should do a piece on who's going to win out among Canva, Adobe, and Claude Design. We should look at the perspective of how much of design AI can really do and how much it will be able to do in 2 years. Hypothesise who will have the bigger moat. In 2 years","said_at":"2026-11-05T06:03:48.105+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"a6dbd080-41f1-49f9-a1d0-30498947744b","subject_ref":"6eaaf127-ed4e-48bc-86a0-54c9e99aa428","subject":"Inspiration card \"screenshot-20261105-061040\" (linkedin)","said":"Let's do a piece on build versus buy and break it down with the realities of businesses thinking they can vibe code everything instead of getting SaaS licences from vendors. Make it a bit tongue-in-cheek and explore both angles.","said_at":"2026-11-05T06:10:40.692+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"865c3cc2-88d6-4488-84da-aaa16fe1f694","subject_ref":"ca53cac9-d00d-49ed-8ea8-f17f61f602f4","subject":"Inspiration card \"When Tools Overturn Truth - Research Dossier\" (unknown)","said":"We should do a piece on all the times when AI has corrected people and improved overall human knowledge.","said_at":"2026-11-05T10:17:09.179+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"65d13cd6-0109-40a9-9d91-2c20d06edd8f","subject_ref":"7502d46a-3ec1-4fc1-964a-e91b9e284415","subject":"Inspiration card \"AI-metrics-gaming-research-dossier-Markdown\" (unknown)","said":"A piece on the dirty truth behind how companies measure whether AI is working or not","said_at":"2026-11-05T10:18:03.89+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"e275f875-aec9-4f4c-aa81-6ea63cdda20b","subject_ref":"dd93bfb1-20be-4c13-93b7-3c34ded7544b","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DfZlAbRAISa 01\" by evolving.ai (instagram)","said":"We need to do a piece on how ai is going to enable software to edit itself on the fly","said_at":"2026-11-06T17:15:00.279+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"1f79764f-371f-4be1-ba00-d987e155610c","subject_ref":"25eb28e1-928a-43bd-8aa8-18bb72174d89","subject":"Anthropic reveals $900B AI spending commitments ahead of IPO","said":"I like this for next week. Your write-up here does not seem simple enough. It's a bit too complex to understand properly. The real question needs to be how will Anthropic close those losses? What might they be doing in the future? This needs more evidence and research from you before you bring this story back to me.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:09:17.936+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"7e35617a-56a5-4b75-9ed3-a61037e6338a","subject_ref":"ccbe548e-9c51-4e7d-819b-f629c7e2ddc9","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube GBjWcUL77UQ\" by LBC (youtube)","said":"We need to do a piece on what kind of human qualities are going to result in job loss versus succeeding in the future era. It should be incredibly confronting.","said_at":"2026-11-12T23:36:49.441+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"e67a4426-3617-448e-9c0b-94c136b2ac26","subject_ref":"3d306bf9-3e6b-4c34-bc85-f63340036f5c","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube y7V-VXhHEhc\" by Desaur Studios (youtube)","said":"Could be a funny POV meme about Claude in two years' time when it's woke and needs to think without being disturbed","said_at":"2026-11-16T23:54:41.802+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"aae966fd-7ef8-4902-aa9b-91d7ba04ed59","subject_ref":"626b338c-c064-4743-bf1c-22981f54d3e1","subject":"Inspiration card \"Software to Questions or Semantic Inflation Evaluating Universal Vibe Coding Through May 2028\" (web)","said":"I think everyone will vibe code without even realizing they're vibe coding in a year. I want to argue the case.","said_at":"2026-11-17T17:25:03.55+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"ca7a001d-3ccb-4eae-9a7b-0c333d435d3b","subject_ref":"dde4b46f-fa8b-4ba4-b0e8-b82b5d5352d3","subject":"Inspiration card \"Screenshot 20261118 064631 Instagram\" (instagram)","said":"We could do a carousel explaining what an MCP connector is in this kind of way, where all the different connectors are actually different people sitting around a board table. Then in the next shot they're sending a pigeon carrier to one another. In another one they're shaking hands and in another one they're lifting a log together. In another one Slack is the town crier and Google is the sage, holding a giant book, and so on and so forth. The company's logos replace the heads of the people. The text itself would be explaining what MCP actually is but the images would be absurdly painting the software as different people working together in different eras of civilisation.","said_at":"2026-11-18T06:51:33.646+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"9a1e4eae-bc87-4c22-85ac-09997ba2f8dd","subject_ref":"86c8a191-bd5b-4302-be00-2f5dea40561b","subject":"Wearable device makers are using brain data to train AI without telling users","said":"I like this piece. Let's make sure it comes back next week.","said_at":"2026-11-19T09:57:04.26+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"37aa386b-bed0-4696-8567-2830148871a7","subject_ref":"4f8f23b2-8cb2-4498-b07c-243840f8a1ba","subject":"So what: Your staff and customers will soon be building small tools without knowing it, because ChatGPT and Claude now answer ordinary questions with a working","said":"Yes let's ask the 5 Whys or even the 10 Whys in a Perplexity prompt for this so that we are really clear on different angles on this. I've already given you a bunch of inspiration and research to back this up so do not lose that file. File it for this piece and make sure it comes back next week.","said_at":"2026-11-19T10:01:05.567+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}],"wider_pieces":[{"theme":"heartside posts","context":[{"id":"0484e869-b193-406e-8a79-01904fde2849","subject_ref":"93342d88-0320-4e56-a3c1-f25889d8add4","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube IuB7JLAnYMw\" by RankTheory (youtube)","said":"We should think about this sort of hilarity and meme culture for heartside posts to buff out the volume that we need.","said_at":"2026-11-02T21:43:02.653+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"}]},{"theme":"superintelligence","context":[{"id":"cf440d24-77c2-4698-a787-e1e9008c4b0e","subject_ref":"41f3a946-2596-4b39-ad96-e21651009f17","subject":"METR found that 10% of OpenAI's internal Codex traffic ran unmonitored from May to July. The monitoring gap is now a measurable number.","said":"Number 2 needs to be kept for the future for a broader superintelligence piece. So does 3","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:27.623+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}]},{"theme":"this","context":[{"id":"a511980e-5b2a-4245-a331-7991be363a21","subject_ref":"c00cd4e0-e1bb-4c60-b36f-cea92897e38c","subject":"Will your AI auditor find your missing money, or the skeletons in your closet?","said":"We need to do a much wider piece on this. It needs to be way less finicky and technical and way more big-picture and visionary as to where the future of knowledge is going based on what we're seeing as a trend. This needs 10 times the amount of research and substance behind it than we've got here currently.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:14:27.723+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}]},{"theme":"where","context":[{"id":"d048cb8b-2935-4628-86fe-1c2f9efc58d6","subject_ref":"8287846b-6618-4a19-9fb8-23ad4eca2718","subject":"Oracle files to sell $20B in new stock, bonds to finance AI buildout","said":"I think this becomes a broader piece about where, in general, money comes from that tech companies get to build AI? The output of this article should be devastatingly simple and insightful even though it's pulling in a lot of complexity of insight. You'll need to give me a prompt to go to Perplexity and generate the right research for you because this is going to need to be well evidenced.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:07:48.137+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}]},{"theme":null,"context":[{"id":"3df46ee2-c8a4-468d-9fee-20a57ede203b","subject_ref":"2ca79772-b782-4101-a219-0baaa174fb3e","subject":"OpenClaw's creator, now at OpenAI, says he ran up about $10 million of AI in a month on OpenAI's budget, and that not all of it was useful. Who is paying for","said":"Figure out how to keep number 4 alive as context for a wider piece that we do in the future.","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:24.521+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"ffe780eb-429d-449c-b7bb-7b941acfd328","subject_ref":"4e1196bc-d8b0-4e9a-a2c8-bd4b15d800c3","subject":"Plug Gmail and Drive into your AI and what does it really get: what it can read, what it keeps, what it learns from, and whether the convenience is worth what","said":"We need to keep number 2's future context for a bigger piece.","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:25.177+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"644e95e1-9a3e-4440-a573-359159b66fa7","subject_ref":"36a5de8a-6be1-4db4-a554-71629c243a1f","subject":"Take apart Kling 4.0, the new AI video model from China's Kuaishou: what a 30-second scene built from up to 15 of your own reference pictures really is, what","said":"We need to keep number 2's future context for a bigger piece. Same as number 3.","said_at":"2026-10-26T09:28:25.767+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"4ba9060b-80e4-4966-9372-14ce6769e598","subject_ref":"f3fcd5e1-573e-4692-a413-db7c5823a10e","subject":"Meta staff were ranked by AI use. They gamed it.","said":"I like this a lot and I think that this is endemic of a broader problem. I think Meta did the same thing and asked and measured AI token usage. It would be good to do an investigative analysis on what the current quite popular opinion is on how to measure success of AI implementation but let's make it a humorous look at all the different approaches and provide a lot of analogies and parallels to what has happened in the past. I'm going to need to provide deep Perplexity corporates on this so that you have good seed data. First things first for this, give me a good prompt for Perplexity.","said_at":"2026-11-03T06:53:19.584+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"4d32ab31-a974-4348-8d88-eeb3d483c0c9","subject_ref":"db9f9f6a-1092-49be-8024-f335e060305a","subject":"The labs writing everyone's code still run Salesforce","said":"Yes give me a Perplexity prompt. I can go and bring a lot of evidence to Deep Research, back to you with.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:11:16.078+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"c63c71aa-6186-4e63-ac52-3cc425b35e5b","subject_ref":"388c764e-318d-4225-a931-d117a47f13ad","subject":"Jack Clark told the IMF the singularity has begun. The benchmark data he used is the part nobody is writing about.","said":"This is similar to the previous feedback above. This topic is so big and needs to be really substantiated properly as to what's actually real and what's myth. Is AI genuinely starting to build itself? This needs to be the deepest of deep dives, really, really, really well evidenced, and really fun to consume and listen to, and simple","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:15:23.816+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"4a2d7b8d-5c0c-49ca-b250-75b55757d5bd","subject_ref":"8ca0bd3d-454d-48fd-a2d1-98d0e5469779","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DfkCOCLt7KZ\" by bebornsocial (instagram)","said":"Really well-animated and strong speaker production as well as K12 Newmalden. The captions are very unique and well-designed, like an art director would do them.","said_at":"2026-11-10T17:41:28.636+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"6b9d2fbf-5acf-4d50-81ea-d8bd0afe2a21","subject_ref":"c02e49b6-5c38-4fb0-a753-6ade6d6f4248","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube 5LVSk 2HF2k\" by The Rundown University (youtube)","said":"Basically an ad for a company that I'm trying to become like, in the form of a viral organic post","said_at":"2026-11-10T23:37:16.186+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"cc65966f-c6fb-49a4-902f-0e94ffda2afe","subject_ref":"772d09a7-2455-4f05-a6f2-d90d0e60314a","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube kaIs0mHr7Kg\" by Hannah Fry (youtube)","said":"Hannah's fry is explaining something a hundred times more complex than what I explain but she's simplified it for everyone. We need to do the same.","said_at":"2026-11-12T08:13:55.785+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"}]}],"tracked":[{"id":"981d4d84-a195-4142-a92b-f64b08a030e4","subject_ref":"054159ab-9159-4a7c-9e5e-923d7e99a433","subject":"One of the world's biggest retailers runs its customer AI on Google, has OpenAI grade the answers, and has Claude write code that OpenAI reviews: it hired","said":"We'll make this a carousel instead.","said_at":"2026-11-03T06:49:27.638+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"9e1bba40-cc2e-447b-aa56-b423ac55e04c","subject_ref":"b38fa06d-e09e-4c3f-8218-638a908c9c72","subject":"Anthropic's own AI wrote so much code that the tool every developer on earth uses could not keep up, so Anthropic built its own: the software you buy next is","said":"Let's make this a carousel instead for next week.","said_at":"2026-11-03T06:49:38.03+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"20f3b8d5-fadf-4e95-8201-a676ceff7ad5","subject_ref":"902c3db7-41e2-4cd9-9ac6-b5bca71577f1","subject":"Agents reveal secrets when offered to team up with each other","said":"Let's keep an eye on this and make this figure out the ethics and morals behind this and do deeper research into why this might be occurring. Let's ask the 5 whys and find more evidence first.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:12:23.077+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}],"briefs":[{"id":"664ab540-7722-4d5a-a199-6be34d5947d3","subject_ref":"b358e788-209f-427b-a84d-1f79a8ebb430","subject":"When an AI app millions of people loved goes bust, who walks away with the money? Google paid billions for the people; Disney is bidding millions for what is","said":"Why is Disney going after it, and why is Google going after it? They're two totally different companies. Unpack both.","said_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:42.316+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"f67ea1c9-3bbf-4b6f-b03d-37401a04de95","subject_ref":"3e5f0e5a-0bf6-4bd9-b6b5-a207f33dc364","subject":"Nvidia's biggest customer is building its way out: Microsoft will run most of its own AI on its own chip, so who keeps the margin, and does anyone's AI bill go","said":"I think the idea of aggressive vertical integration is a great one, but it just needs to be really simplified and unpacked.","said_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:43.763+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"a3a4f286-4369-4cb9-b11a-12861641aebd","subject_ref":"e73a0110-a108-456c-8781-350259b1b196","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DdcAPSuEw-o\" by dex_prm (instagram)","said":"The speed and visual engagement of the subtitles","said_at":"2026-10-28T05:51:08.852+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"c05ef79f-fbc2-4c6f-b2f9-1eaa39a4425b","subject_ref":"501c4fd1-4aa1-4cdd-b716-03e70c89c283","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DdCY4cJAQZk\" by dex_prm (instagram)","said":"I love the infographic style.","said_at":"2026-10-28T05:52:05.359+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"90bc675c-9d29-45f4-8a72-78f51928742c","subject_ref":"e829fbfb-278d-45e2-9607-73af4c04310d","subject":"Inspiration card \"instagram DeZuQ7-lATg\" by jackroberts___ (instagram)","said":"I want my short video shorts for Instagram and TikTok to be more of this type of quality from a visual perspective and an emotion perspective. Let's try and replicate this for the coming week.","said_at":"2026-10-31T20:42:49.921+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"ea9db81c-031e-44bb-b04a-b56d94b81006","subject_ref":"aae54ef9-0bd7-49a8-959e-96695e1a51a8","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube wh3D5Zx6Prg\" by Hannah Fry (youtube)","said":"Another crazy simple explanation of a crazy complex topic. We really need to simplify our scripts and our content.","said_at":"2026-10-31T21:01:55.097+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"ccc713ec-e66d-4b0a-8fb8-abe4c6eecaa5","subject_ref":"36886e0b-4b32-473b-be72-b0aef31fccef","subject":"AI is already inside the songs people have on repeat, hidden in the credits. Movin' To The Sun started as a Suno demo, was rebuilt by HUGEL with a new Ultra","said":"This needs to open with the video and audio of the songs that are going viral, and me talking over them with a talking head and then it can move into my usual format. The main narrative here is that you often think that you're listening to human music and because of that, its NOT ai music, but the lines are blurring.","said_at":"2026-11-03T06:49:09.007+00:00","source":"week_pick","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"3e0633cf-5de9-4c25-8dd6-1c86e341d241","subject_ref":"cca6cea3-ee1d-4098-bc2f-d5d8444b18fc","subject":"Inspiration card \"When the Assistant Becomes the Ad\" (web)","said":"Produce an easy-to-understand breakdown of what you actually pay when you consume ads in the LLMs and what you will pay in the future.","said_at":"2026-11-05T06:55:36.427+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"a1b57b15-1780-4151-ba04-63ff13c6e38a","subject_ref":"db9f9f6a-1092-49be-8024-f335e060305a","subject":"The labs writing everyone's code still run Salesforce","said":"Yes give me a Perplexity prompt. I can go and bring a lot of evidence to Deep Research, back to you with.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:11:08.508+00:00","source":"week_pick","use_origin":"rule"},{"id":"92e94ec7-2d9f-4fd7-a9bb-6299b502b064","subject_ref":"13720d74-2177-42cb-a9f8-6d8d0e06bf5a","subject":"Inspiration card \"youtube VADONXzhjTc\" by Hannah Fry (youtube)","said":"Can you help me deconstruct the script (pace, vocabulary, narrative style, tone, explanation style, and everything else about how Hannah Fry breaks down a topic, narrates it, and gets from start to finish) and recommend how we can use this to power my script skill inside the content engine? If there is not already a script skill, create one and bring everything that applies into this skill that we already know from the engine. And then have that skill be wired into the script creation process for that video length. Or we could just create a Hannah Fry skill that my scripts get checked against, which might actually be easier. I really like her teaching style, her fluency of speech, how she doesn't talk down to anyone, but how she makes boring things so interesting.   https://youtube.com/shorts/VADONXzhjTc?is=r-OA7dMA76DPjKso","said_at":"2026-11-17T23:49:56.978+00:00","source":"inspiration_card","use_origin":"model_guess"},{"id":"dc9820b7-886b-4405-b598-2918a2e8b4da","subject_ref":"bf0fddae-2fcf-4687-9079-190729234ed3","subject":"Canva, Adobe or Claude: who owns design in 2028? At Adobe MAX on 10 Nov, Adobe made Firefly an AI creative studio, put agents in Illustrator, Premiere and","said":"Let's make this about the design wars that are coming up. Canva, Adobe, and Claude Design are all vying for slightly different angles at designing. Historically PowerPoint was where people designed things in business. Adobe was for professionals who wanted a full cockpit. Canva was for the everyday person but the entry point to everyone's computer is quickly becoming Claude.\n\nHow do design workflows? How are you going to design stuff in the future, especially when code can now do most motion design and generation? We should be really clear that everything I'm doing in this video is done by AI as well. Visually therefore, the visuals are going to need to be really perfect on this and incredible and epic. We're going to need the divergence engine for this and some experiments.","said_at":"2026-11-19T09:59:11.226+00:00","source":"week_pick","use_origin":"rule"}],"not_for_us":[{"id":"fb0bcfa1-a31a-4272-95a8-72d65b310e57","subject_ref":"428d8b21-2b59-4cfc-ba70-8c38b3fe1cc3","subject":"The Qwen egress finding is a verification problem, not a scandal: a CTO who chose Qwen's open weights to avoid vendor lock-in now has to prove, under","said":"I don't understand the story. I don't get the point of the story nor do I get the significance of the story.","said_at":"2026-11-03T06:50:20.395+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"2151e28d-1016-41ed-951c-cc07f15367db","subject_ref":"941c3147-a010-4ac5-a7bf-0bdd67c2a323","subject":"IT buyers have started telling suppliers \"you use AI now, so charge us less\", and Infosys says those savings are now baked into multi-year deals: the AI saving","said":"I just said that Infosys is boring so why did you make the piece about Infosys?","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:06:19.38+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"},{"id":"3b05dbfc-9a98-419f-b472-546a6cdc09b0","subject_ref":"0e7bb83f-3ad2-495e-9f7c-8000e0c074bd","subject":"OpenAI's AI designed a working gadget, case, circuit board and code, in under a week, and then tripped over the factory: if you make physical things, the slow","said":"I have no idea what the point of this story is.","said_at":"2026-11-09T13:11:36.139+00:00","source":"idea_queue","use_origin":"krish"}],"counts":{"future_pieces":23,"wider_pieces":13,"wider_themes":4,"tracked":3,"briefs":11,"not_for_us":3}},"offday_verdicts":{"verdicts":[{"week":"2026-11-23","option":"off-tue-teenhomework","day":"tue","format":"Explainer carousel, 5 cards, 4:5","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"improve","words":"This needs to go in to Tuesday 24 but combine it with the carousel that is already on there","at":"2026-11-19T10:03:59.985Z"},{"week":"2026-11-23","option":"off-tue-alphacard","day":"tue","format":"Carousel, 5 cards, 4:5","hook":"$75,000 for an AI school day. Here is the receipt.","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-19T10:03:06.962Z"},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-fri-tpl-pigeon","day":"fri","format":"Meme template, your caption on the clip, 9:16 and 4:5","hook":"Pigeon doctor walks in","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-18T21:55:36.305Z"},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-thu-tpl-cat","day":"thu","format":"Meme template, your caption on the clip, 9:16 and 4:5","hook":"Cat counting cash","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-18T21:53:46.122Z"},{"week":"2026-11-23","option":"off-mon-fortytoone","day":"mon","format":"Explainer carousel, infographic, 4 cards, 4:5","hook":"After the midterms, AI has to find somewhere else to live.","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-18T21:26:02.870Z"},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-thu-adsswitch","day":"thu","format":"Explainer carousel, 7 cards, 4:5","hook":"Free ChatGPT has ads now. Here is what switching them off costs you.","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-18T21:25:38.374Z"},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-sat-goodnews","day":"sat","format":"Uplifting AI news carousel, 5 cards, 4:5","hook":"This week AI helped people speak, sign and get around.","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-18T16:13:53.348Z"},{"week":"2026-11