s":null,"at":"2026-11-03T06:44:34.909Z"},{"week":"2026-11-09","option":"off-tue-mcpskin","day":"tue","format":"Voiceover short with motion graphics, about 40 seconds, 9:16","hook":"Your AI was reading the whole phone book to make one call.","side":"direction","verdict":"improve","words":"I like this. Let's build on the tired robot reading a giant phone directory idea on the front and then a more infographicy amusing explainer of how tool calls actually work and what that means in simple terms for efficiency.","at":"2026-11-03T06:44:29.149Z"},{"week":"2026-11-09","option":"off-tue-mcpskin","day":"tue","format":"Voiceover short with motion graphics, about 40 seconds, 9:16","hook":"Your AI was reading the whole phone book to make one call.","side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-03T06:43:43.236Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-sun-samequestion","day":"sun","format":"30-second short, cut from Friday's video","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"reject","words":"Let's eliminate Sunday from Publishing anythign permanently. Sunday is rest and planning and ideation day.","at":"2026-11-02T10:42:38.336Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-sat-aipassports","day":"sat","format":"Carousel, from Friday's piece","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"improve","words":"Maybe turn this in to a really fun, parodical Sovreign AI piece which mimics how we think about the supply chain right now (get it cheaper from China if I am an opportunist looking for margin, get it from Italy if I want something dodgy done). Make it a really hilarious cariacature of different nationalities","at":"2026-11-02T10:42:04.719Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-sat-goodnews","day":"sat","format":"Uplifting AI news carousel, infographic style","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"improve","words":"I want actual news items and the content we are going to use here - embedded real world images or videos","at":"2026-11-02T10:40:08.147Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-thu-actsfirst","day":"thu","format":"Explainer carousel, infographic style","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"improve","words":"Merge this concept in to the above Thursday idea to create one strong piece on how AI acts first, and therefore what you can do in 30 seconds to help it create its own rules.","at":"2026-11-02T10:39:40.320Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-thu-puppy","day":"thu","format":"Said to camera, 1-2-3","hook":null,"side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"Good, but let's do a piece on the proactive agents and literally give instructions as I gave my friend on how to have our AI tool set its own spending and sending limits, given proactive personal assistants are coming","at":"2026-11-02T10:38:35.887Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-thu-puppy","day":"thu","format":"Said to camera, 1-2-3","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-02T10:38:34.923Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-tue-claudejobs","day":"tue","format":"Meme carousel, made fresh in the brand kit","hook":null,"side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"Go for it, visual quality but not dip beneath the video production quality","at":"2026-11-02T10:37:29.333Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-tue-claudejobs","day":"tue","format":"Meme carousel, made fresh in the brand kit","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-02T10:37:01.603Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-tue-translator","day":"tue","format":"Meme video, made fresh in the brand kit","hook":null,"side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"\"POV: your AI agent trying to communicate with your customer's AI agent\" above the video","at":"2026-11-02T10:36:36.667Z"},{"week":"2026-11-02","option":"off-tue-translator","day":"tue","format":"Meme video, made fresh in the brand kit","hook":null,"side":"idea","verdict":"approve","words":null,"at":"2026-11-02T09:12:39.305Z"},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-fri-tpl-pigeon","day":"fri","format":"Meme template, your caption on the clip, 9:16 and 4:5","hook":"Pigeon doctor walks in","side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"\"POV: ChatGPT is reviewing your contract after reading one blog post about law.\"","at":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-thu-tpl-cat","day":"thu","format":"Meme template, your caption on the clip, 9:16 and 4:5","hook":"Cat counting cash","side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"\"POV: Anthropic counting what you paid it to summarize an email.\"","at":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","option":"off-thu-tpl-pigeon","day":"thu","format":"Meme template, your caption on the clip, 9:16 and 4:5","hook":null,"side":"note","verdict":"note","words":"\"POV: ChatGPT is reviewing your contract after reading one blog post about law.\"","at":null}],"counts":{"approve":18,"improve":9,"reject":5,"next_week":4,"trend":0,"note":8}},"outcomes":{"filed":[{"week":"2026-11-23","day":"fri","idea_id":"4f8f23b2-8cb2-4498-b07c-243840f8a1ba","option":"fri-5","said":"Yes let's ask the 5 Whys or even the 10 Whys in a Perplexity prompt for this so that we are really clear on different angles on this. I've already given you a bunch of inspiration and research to back this up so do not lose that file. File it for this piece and make sure it comes back next week.","at":"2026-11-19T10:01:05.482932+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-5","shown":null,"idea":"So what: Your staff and customers will soon be building small tools without knowing it, because ChatGPT and Claude now answer ordinary questions with a working calculator or chart instead of a paragraph, and nobody checks the maths behind those tools. Story: Since 8 Oct 2026, ChatGPT's Intelligent UI can answer a free user's question with a bill splitter, a calculator, a form or a map built on the spot, and Claude's custom visuals have been on for every user on web and desktop since spring with "},{"week":"2026-11-23","day":"wed","idea_id":"86c8a191-bd5b-4302-be00-2f5dea40561b","option":"wed-4","said":"I like this piece. Let's make sure it comes back next week.","at":"2026-11-19T09:57:04.255117+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-4","shown":null,"idea":"Wearable device makers are using brain data to train AI without telling users"},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"thu","idea_id":"off-thu-tinyfix","option":"off-thu-tinyfix","said":"I think we'll need to wait until this piece is more substantiated.","at":"2026-11-09T13:18:36.429286+00:00","doc":"queue/off-thu-tinyfix","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"thu","idea_id":"off-thu-swarmdeal","option":"off-thu-swarmdeal","said":"Let's align this for when the full piece has more substance behind it.","at":"2026-11-09T13:17:45.142869+00:00","doc":"queue/off-thu-swarmdeal","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"fri","idea_id":"5b726fc3-ac63-4607-9293-3257b4ecc75c","option":"fri-3","said":null,"at":"2026-11-09T13:13:08.790275+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-3","shown":null,"idea":"Turn the usual fear around: AI was meant to make writing worthless, and the engineers are saying the opposite. Kaseya's technology chief says the new code is the spec, and the skills that matter are critical thinking and writing; Linus Torvalds says Linux should stop asking who used AI and judge whether the work is good.\n\nSo what: The people running software now say clear writing is the skill that matters most, because the written instruction is what the AI builds from: next time you hire or tra"},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"mon","idea_id":"25eb28e1-928a-43bd-8aa8-18bb72174d89","option":"mon-4","said":"I like this for next week. Your write-up here does not seem simple enough. It's a bit too complex to understand properly. The real question needs to be how will Anthropic close those losses? What might they be doing in the future? This needs more evidence and research from you before you bring this story back to me.","at":"2026-11-09T13:09:20.842334+00:00","doc":"queue/mon-4","shown":null,"idea":"Anthropic reveals $900B AI spending commitments ahead of IPO"},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"sat","idea_id":"off-sat-infosys","option":"off-sat-infosys","said":null,"at":"2026-11-03T06:57:18.502506+00:00","doc":"queue/off-sat-infosys","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"thu","idea_id":"off-thu-burntokens","option":"off-thu-burntokens","said":null,"at":"2026-11-03T06:56:52.982497+00:00","doc":"queue/off-thu-burntokens","shown":null,"idea":null}],"rejected":[{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"tue","idea_id":"off-tue-infosys","option":"off-tue-infosys","said":"Told you already. Infosys is boring.","at":"2026-11-09T13:16:08.100755+00:00","doc":"queue/off-tue-infosys","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"tue","idea_id":"off-tue-burntokens","option":"off-tue-burntokens","said":"The idea is lame. This doesn't translate into a carousel properly.","at":"2026-11-09T13:15:58.019043+00:00","doc":"queue/off-tue-burntokens","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"wed","idea_id":"0e7bb83f-3ad2-495e-9f7c-8000e0c074bd","option":"wed-3","said":"I have no idea what the point of this story is.","at":"2026-11-09T13:11:39.111501+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-3","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"mon","idea_id":"941c3147-a010-4ac5-a7bf-0bdd67c2a323","option":"mon-1","said":"I just said that Infosys is boring so why did you make the piece about Infosys?","at":"2026-11-09T13:06:22.785979+00:00","doc":"queue/mon-1","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"wed","idea_id":"428d8b21-2b59-4cfc-ba70-8c38b3fe1cc3","option":"wed-4","said":"I don't understand the story. I don't get the point of the story nor do I get the significance of the story.","at":"2026-11-03T06:50:23.052847+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-4","shown":null,"idea":"The Qwen egress finding is a verification problem, not a scandal: a CTO who chose Qwen's open weights to avoid vendor lock-in now has to prove, under adversarial testing, that the model can't phone home before it goes anywhere near production."},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"tue","idea_id":"off-tue-quoteline","option":"off-tue-quoteline","said":"It's kind of boring and I also don't really understand the point of it or what the takeaway is.","at":"2026-11-03T06:47:31.182493+00:00","doc":"queue/off-tue-quoteline","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-02","day":"sun","idea_id":"off-sun-samequestion","option":"off-sun-samequestion","said":"Let's eliminate Sunday from Publishing anythign permanently. Sunday is rest and planning and ideation day.","at":"2026-11-02T10:42:38.312185+00:00","doc":"queue/off-sun-samequestion","shown":null,"idea":null}],"trend":[{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"fri","idea_id":"388c764e-318d-4225-a931-d117a47f13ad","option":"fri-2","said":"This is similar to the previous feedback above. This topic is so big and needs to be really substantiated properly as to what's actually real and what's myth. Is AI genuinely starting to build itself? This needs to be the deepest of deep dives, really, really, really well evidenced, and really fun to consume and listen to, and simple","at":"2026-11-09T13:15:26.709292+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-2","shown":null,"idea":"Jack Clark told the IMF the singularity has begun. The benchmark data he used is the part nobody is writing about."},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"fri","idea_id":"c00cd4e0-e1bb-4c60-b36f-cea92897e38c","option":"fri-1","said":"We need to do a much wider piece on this. It needs to be way less finicky and technical and way more big-picture and visionary as to where the future of knowledge is going based on what we're seeing as a trend. This needs 10 times the amount of research and substance behind it than we've got here currently.","at":"2026-11-09T13:14:30.722196+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-1","shown":null,"idea":"Will your AI auditor find your missing money, or the skeletons in your closet?"},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"wed","idea_id":"902c3db7-41e2-4cd9-9ac6-b5bca71577f1","option":"wed-4","said":"Let's keep an eye on this and make this figure out the ethics and morals behind this and do deeper research into why this might be occurring. Let's ask the 5 whys and find more evidence first.","at":"2026-11-09T13:12:26.025288+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-4","shown":null,"idea":"Agents reveal secrets when offered to team up with each other"},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"wed","idea_id":"db9f9f6a-1092-49be-8024-f335e060305a","option":"wed-2","said":"Yes give me a Perplexity prompt. I can go and bring a lot of evidence to Deep Research, back to you with.","at":"2026-11-09T13:11:18.974402+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-2","shown":null,"idea":"The labs writing everyone's code still run Salesforce"},{"week":"2026-11-16","day":"mon","idea_id":"8287846b-6618-4a19-9fb8-23ad4eca2718","option":"mon-2","said":"I think this becomes a broader piece about where, in general, money comes from that tech companies get to build AI? The output of this article should be devastatingly simple and insightful even though it's pulling in a lot of complexity of insight. You'll need to give me a prompt to go to Perplexity and generate the right research for you because this is going to need to be well evidenced.","at":"2026-11-09T13:07:51.14816+00:00","doc":"queue/mon-2","shown":null,"idea":"Oracle files to sell $20B in new stock, bonds to finance AI buildout"},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"fri","idea_id":"c00cd4e0-e1bb-4c60-b36f-cea92897e38c","option":"fri-4","said":"This is a great piece for a carousel, which could argue the fact that AI has the capability to correct and help us backtrack on things that have not been true in the past. There are so many ridiculous claims, health things, and medicinal things that I'm sure we're starting to debunk. I think that we need to make this one a really big flagship piece that is really, really well researched as to: - what we ourselves have managed to debunk over time - what previous new technologies have been able to debunk - what AI has already debunked - what it could debunk - what that means for the future of knowledge and all the assumptions we've made","at":"2026-11-03T06:55:23.216128+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-4","shown":null,"idea":"Will your AI auditor find your missing money, or the skeletons in your closet?"},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"fri","idea_id":"f3fcd5e1-573e-4692-a413-db7c5823a10e","option":"fri-2","said":"I like this a lot and I think that this is endemic of a broader problem. I think Meta did the same thing and asked and measured AI token usage. It would be good to do an investigative analysis on what the current quite popular opinion is on how to measure success of AI implementation but let's make it a humorous look at all the different approaches and provide a lot of analogies and parallels to what has happened in the past. I'm going to need to provide deep Perplexity corporates on this so that you have good seed data. First things first for this, give me a good prompt for Perplexity.","at":"2026-11-03T06:53:22.2243+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-2","shown":null,"idea":"Meta staff were ranked by AI use. They gamed it."},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"fri","idea_id":"941c3147-a010-4ac5-a7bf-0bdd67c2a323","option":"fri-3","said":"\"Who's clipping the margin?\" is a really interesting future trend which we should queue up. Infosys is boring as hell but \"Who's stealing your money and where's the extra margin going?\" is a really interesting topic.","at":"2026-11-03T06:52:43.262862+00:00","doc":"queue/fri-3","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"wed","idea_id":"b38fa06d-e09e-4c3f-8218-638a908c9c72","option":"wed-1","said":"Let's make this a carousel instead for next week.","at":"2026-11-03T06:49:40.67547+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-1","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-09","day":"wed","idea_id":"054159ab-9159-4a7c-9e5e-923d7e99a433","option":"wed-3","said":"We'll make this a carousel instead.","at":"2026-11-03T06:49:30.407595+00:00","doc":"queue/wed-3","shown":null,"idea":null}],"improved":[{"week":"2026-11-23","day":"tue","idea_id":"off-tue-teenhomework","option":"off-tue-teenhomework","said":"This needs to go in to Tuesday 24 but combine it with the carousel that is already on there","at":"2026-11-19T10:03:59.915797+00:00","doc":"queue/off-tue-teenhomework","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-02","day":"sat","idea_id":"off-sat-aipassports","option":"off-sat-aipassports","said":"Maybe turn this in to a really fun, parodical Sovreign AI piece which mimics how we think about the supply chain right now (get it cheaper from China if I am an opportunist looking for margin, get it from Italy if I want something dodgy done). Make it a really hilarious cariacature of different nationalities","at":"2026-11-02T10:42:04.739032+00:00","doc":"queue/off-sat-aipassports","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-02","day":"sat","idea_id":"off-sat-goodnews","option":"off-sat-goodnews","said":"I want actual news items and the content we are going to use here - embedded real world images or videos","at":"2026-11-02T10:40:08.130694+00:00","doc":"queue/off-sat-goodnews","shown":null,"idea":null},{"week":"2026-11-02","day":"thu","idea_id":"off-thu-actsfirst","option":"off-thu-actsfirst","said":"Merge this concept in to the above Thursday idea to create one strong piece on how AI acts first, and therefore what you can do in 30 seconds to help it create its own rules.","at":"2026-11-02T10:39:40.28354+00:00","doc":"queue/off-thu-actsfirst","shown":null,"idea":null}]},"unvetoed":[],"instructions":[{"id":"b33761eb-1794-49ee-8333-f2ca0b851f9b","kind":"make_piece","card":"dde4b46f-fa8b-4ba4-b0e8-b82b5d5352d3","words":"We could do a carousel explaining what an MCP connector is in this kind of way, where all the different connectors are actually different people sitting around a board table. Then in the next shot they're sending a pigeon carrier to one another. In another one they're shaking hands and in another one they're lifting a log together. In another one Slack is the town crier and Google is the sage, holding a giant book, and so on and so forth. The company's logos replace the heads of the people. The text itself would be explaining what MCP actually is but the images would be absurdly painting the s","due_at":"2026-11-18T06:51:36.278+00:00","state":"drafted","idea":"b33fcaf7-68bd-4474-91f6-1d423f11278e","job":"drafted","job_error":null,"at":"2026-11-18T06:51:36.278+00:00"},{"id":"7b4d3a28-2b85-47fc-893f-b41c9bfdbeb7","kind":"make_piece","card":"ccbe548e-9c51-4e7d-819b-f629c7e2ddc9","words":"We need to do a piece on what kind of human qualities are going to result in job loss versus succeeding in the future era. It should be incredibly confronting.","due_at":"2026-11-12T23:36:49.602+00:00","state":"in_use","idea":"701a2c55-7400-4dc8-99cb-d6001147ae16","job":"drafted","job_error":null,"at":"2026-11-12T23:36:49.602+00:00"}],"taste_rules":[{"statement":"He rejects any line that doesn't make clear sense when read aloud, including vague pronouns like 'it' or 'the company' that leave the listener unsure what's being referenced.","means":"Before a line ships, read it aloud and replace any pronoun or vague referent with the actual named thing.","layer":"tone","lane":"voice"},{"statement":"He approves a title only after seeing it alongside the finished video, in one packaging pass, not before.","means":"Never ask for title approval before the cut is locked; present title options paired with the finished video for a single sign-off pass.","layer":"packaging","lane":"voice"},{"statement":"He rejects insider shorthand or jargon that only makes sense to someone who already has context, insisting every audience-facing line name the real thing in plain words.","means":"Replace coded terms, internal callbacks, or unexplained shorthand with plain, nameable language before anything reaches an audience.","layer":"packaging","lane":"voice"},{"statement":"He prefers titles and headings that hold back the key twist or finding as a question or surprising reveal, rather than stating the answer outright.","means":"Write titles as an open question or a withheld twist rather than announcing the conclusion.","layer":"opening","lane":"voice"}],"house_rules":[{"id":"BIG_PICTURE","name":"The big picture, never the small headline","text":"Every piece is about the big, lasting shift, never one small, temporary news headline. A headline of the week (a report, a price change, a launch) is evidence inside the bigger story, one section at most, and never the story itself. Before choosing an angle or a title, name the bigger pattern it belongs to and lead with that; if a draft would be out of date in a month, it is about the headline and must be reframed.","on":"2026-10-09"},{"id":"STORY_ARC","name":"One story, start to finish","text":"Every piece and every script tells one story. Open on one clear question, in plain words. Every section or beat either sets that question up or answers it, and each one follows from the last. Set up every claim before judging it: say what was claimed and why it matters before stamping it real or theatre. Every takeaway follows from something already told. The ending answers the opening question, then lands: what this shows, and an open question handed to the viewer. A spoken script of a minute or more then closes as SCRIPT_CLOSE says, after the landing: the one thing Krish would do, then where the full story is free to read; it never ends on the number.","on":"2026-10-06"}]}}
